{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794851704004,"sessionID":"ses_e1a82d918ffeSg4o2dc6d2Zt3H","part":{"partID":"prt_1e57f6d9c0023eBl1L3wezLHF9","sessionID":"ses_e1a82d918ffeSg4o2dc6d2Zt3H","messageID":"msg_1e57f4d73001eAjhK3fvhkExxl","type":"tool","id":"call_755c1d4f5e62475098b4d475","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && grep -rn \"A runtime name outside\\|the ones already there\" --include=\"*.txt\" --include=\"*.md\" --include=\"*.yaml\" --include=\"*.json\" .skilled | grep -v \"lineages/\" | head -30"},"output":".skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-install.yaml:58:    - \"Ask: When --root or --runtimes is missing, ask once for the target repo's absolute path, runtimes (claude, opencode, codex, cursor, devin, pi, vibe, dsh, or the ones already there), link shape (auto, whole or merge) and instruction file (embed or link). Stop for the answers.\"\n.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-install-presentation.txt:58:2) Runtimes: claude, opencode, codex, cursor, devin, pi, vibe, dsh, or \"the ones already there\"\n.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-install-presentation.txt:71:| `the ones already there`, empty, `any` | no `--runtimes` | The engine keeps the runtimes its own detection finds in the root, and always links `.skilled` |\n.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-install-presentation.txt:78:A runtime name outside claude, codex, cursor, devin, dsh, opencode, pi and vibe or the ones already there, a shape outside the three, or an instruction word outside the two is not guessed. Ask that one question again with the accepted values. When the engine refuses a root, show its `ERROR:` line as it printed and ask question 1 again.\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":".skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-install.yaml:58:    - \"Ask: When --root or --runtimes is missing, ask once for the target repo's absolute path, runtimes (claude, opencode, codex, cursor, devin, pi, vibe, dsh, or the ones already there), link shape (auto, whole or merge) and instruction file (embed or link). Stop for the answers.\"\n.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-install-presentation.txt:58:2) Runtimes: claude, opencode, codex, cursor, devin, pi, vibe, dsh, or \"the ones already there\"\n.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-install-presentation.txt:71:| `the ones already there`, empty, `any` | no `--runtimes` | The engine keeps the runtimes its own detection finds in the root, and always links `.skilled` |\n.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-install-presentation.txt:78:A runtime name outside claude, codex, cursor, devin, dsh, opencode, pi and vibe or the ones already there, a shape outside the three, or an instruction word outside the two is not guessed. Ask that one question again with the accepted values. When the engine refuses a root, show its `ERROR:` line as it printed and ask question 1 again.\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && grep -rn \\\"A runtime name outside\\\\|the ones already there\\\" --include=\\\"*.txt\\\" --include=\\\"*.md\\\" --include=\\\"*.yaml\\\" --include=\\\"*.json\\\" .skilled | grep -v \\\"lineages/\\\" | head -30\"}"},"time":{"start":1794851696028,"end":1794851704004}}}}
