{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794851842590,"sessionID":"ses_e1a82d918ffeSg4o2dc6d2Zt3H","part":{"partID":"prt_1e581a2a4001UpRRb7N6R1D4wD","sessionID":"ses_e1a82d918ffeSg4o2dc6d2Zt3H","messageID":"msg_1e5814bb7001dwad8sxQtg75v0","type":"tool","id":"call_482196da53cd4068bb56f1f9","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && grep -rn \"dsh row\\|no dsh\\|DSH\" .skilled/commands/doctor --include=\"*.md\" --include=\"*.txt\" --include=\"*.yaml\" --include=\"*.cjs\" --include=\"*.json\" | grep -v tests/ | head -20; echo \"===ROUTER===\"; grep -n \"runtime\" .skilled/commands/doctor/install.md | head -20"},"output":".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agent-roster-mirror-check.cjs:13:// DSH and Vibe by generated files in their own dialects. Nothing in the runtimes\n.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/git-setup-check.cjs:77:// DSH loads one plugin bundle, and an adapter link in it runs only when the bundle\n.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/git-setup-check.cjs:79:const DSH_BUNDLE = '.dsh/plugins/repo-guards/index.mjs';\n.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/git-setup-check.cjs:1483:// The DSH adapter is a link into the hook library, and Node resolves a link to its real\n.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/git-setup-check.cjs:1498:  const bundle = readRepoFile(path.join(repoRoot, DSH_BUNDLE));\n.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/git-setup-check.cjs:1500:    return { status: 'broken', detail: `cannot read ${DSH_BUNDLE}: ${bundle.problem || 'missing'}` };\n.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/git-setup-check.cjs:1505:    return { status: 'broken', detail: `${DSH_BUNDLE} does not register the git-preflight advisory adapter` };\n.skilled/commands/doctor/runtime-mirrors.md:59:The workflow runs every mirror checker in its check-only form (runtime command and agent links, the Codex and Pi prompt and agent mirrors, the DSH and Vibe skill, prompt and agent mirrors, the agent roster, the command catalog, and the Codex hook install) and reports each surface as in sync, drifting with its repair command, or unable to run. It writes nothing.\n.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-git-setup.yaml:41:  tool: \"--tool=<name> names the AI tool running the check: claude, codex, devin, cursor, opencode, pi or dsh. A DSH run is judged by its repo-guards bundle: the adapter link .dsh/plugins/repo-guards/adapters/git-preflight-advisory.mjs must resolve, the bundle entry must import and call its register function, and the real adapter must register tools/post-execute and import git-rule-checks.mjs. For other tools, that tool's adapter must register the advisory under its own pre-tool event for its shell tool, and an OpenCode or Pi adapter must register its event handler and import git-rule-checks.mjs. Every other adapter is checked the same way and fails only when its file exists without the registration. Without --tool, and outside Claude Code, the row is UNKNOWN and names --tool.\"\n.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-runtime-mirrors.yaml:169:  STATUS=OK when every checker reports in sync, or n/a for a DSH or Vibe row while its runtime tree is absent, and the\n.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-runtime-mirrors.yaml:188:  While .dsh/ is absent the three DSH rows read n/a (no .dsh/ tree), and while .vibe/ is absent the three\n===ROUTER===\n3:argument-hint: \"[--root <dir>] [--runtimes <list>] [--json] | list | ?\"\n18:This command never runs a target that writes, and never adds an argument to a printed command beyond the values the operator gave: `--root`, `--runtimes`, the link shape and the instruction choice.\n37:- `--root <dir>` is the target repo's absolute path. `--runtimes <list>` is a comma list drawn from `claude,opencode,codex,cursor,devin,pi,vibe,dsh`; without it the engine keeps the runtimes its own detection finds in the root. `--json` prints one JSON object and nothing else.\n39:- The link shape and the instruction choice have no flag, so both are always answe