with its repair command, or unable to run. It writes nothing.\n.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-git-setup.yaml:41:  tool: \"--tool=<name> names the AI tool running the check: claude, codex, devin, cursor, opencode, pi or dsh. A DSH run is judged by its repo-guards bundle: the adapter link .dsh/plugins/repo-guards/adapters/git-preflight-advisory.mjs must resolve, the bundle entry must import and call its register function, and the real adapter must register tools/post-execute and import git-rule-checks.mjs. For other tools, that tool's adapter must register the advisory under its own pre-tool event for its shell tool, and an OpenCode or Pi adapter must register its event handler and import git-rule-checks.mjs. Every other adapter is checked the same way and fails only when its file exists without the registration. Without --tool, and outside Claude Code, the row is UNKNOWN and names --tool.\"\n.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-runtime-mirrors.yaml:169:  STATUS=OK when every checker reports in sync, or n/a for a DSH or Vibe row while its runtime tree is absent, and the\n.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-runtime-mirrors.yaml:188:  While .dsh/ is absent the three DSH rows read n/a (no .dsh/ tree), and while .vibe/ is absent the three\n===ROUTER===\n3:argument-hint: \"[--root <dir>] [--runtimes <list>] [--json] | list | ?\"\n18:This command never runs a target that writes, and never adds an argument to a printed command beyond the values the operator gave: `--root`, `--runtimes`, the link shape and the instruction choice.\n37:- `--root <dir>` is the target repo's absolute path. `--runtimes <list>` is a comma list drawn from `claude,opencode,codex,cursor,devin,pi,vibe,dsh`; without it the engine keeps the runtimes its own detection finds in the root. `--json` prints one JSON object and nothing else.\n39:- The link shape and the instruction choice have no flag, so both are always answered at the prompt. A `--root` or `--runtimes` already passed drops its ow