{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794852019270,"sessionID":"ses_e1a82d918ffeSg4o2dc6d2Zt3H","part":{"partID":"prt_1e584598d0012y1MSuqKkWxc6b","sessionID":"ses_e1a82d918ffeSg4o2dc6d2Zt3H","messageID":"msg_1e58446e4001HSgiD4dO4YVFq2","type":"tool","id":"call_e877accac6aa434680726cd4","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/039-main-sk-doc-routing-repair && grep -n \"quote\\|doctor\\|runtime\\|REQ-\" spec.md | sed -n '1,80p'"},"output":"45:- Main's commits `fad83abd791` (root guide and skill README intents), `f6f242c1392` (hook, plugin and runtime folder README intents) and `3dc90eb8e01` (named hook README phrases)\n58:Main's README intents gave sk-doc words that other skills own. The named hook phrases, such as `git-hooks-check hook readme`, give sk-doc the words `git` and `hooks`, so \"git hooks\", \"git rules\" and \"git standards\" route nowhere. `hook mirror readme` and `runtime folder readme` give it `runtime` and `mirror`, so \"runtime mirror drift\" tops sk-doc instead of `/doctor:runtime-mirrors`. One ratchet row's native top moved from mcp-tooling to sk-doc, and the independent holdout fell to 48 of 63 against a baseline of 49. Main also changed the sk-doc metadata without recompiling the skill graph, so the strict freshness check reports signal drift.\n67:$ npx vitest run      (advisor runtime, merged HEAD e91faf28b8c, and clean origin/main 2005499d504)\n69:FAIL doctor-bridge-isolation > git hooks / git standards / git rules / git hooks broken\n70:FAIL doctor-routing-slice: doctor-a-10 \"runtime mirror drift\" top=sk-doc, doctor-control-11/12/14 top=null\n74:$ node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/skill-graph-freshness.cjs --strict\n88:- Narrow the runtime and mirror README phrases the same way\n92:- Fix review pass ten's two P1: single-quoted command names, and the doctor install wording the merge left out of step with its test\n107:| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/skill-graph.json` | Modify | Recompiled graph |\n108:| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts` | Modify | Drop a single quote that opens a command name |\n109:| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` | Modify | Quote cases |\n110:| `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-install-presentation.txt`, `doctor-install.yaml`, `scripts/tests/doctor-install-contract.test.cjs` | Modify | Name the eight manifest runtimes and drop the stale DSH sentence |\n124:| REQ-001 | The advisor suite reports 0 failed with `AI_SESSION_CHILD` unset and set to 1, and `FLOOR` prints 24/44, 0/35 and 2/44 |\n125:| REQ-002 | \"git hooks\", \"git rules\", \"git standards\" and \"git hooks broken\" route to sk-git, and \"runtime mirror drift\" tops `command-doctor-runtime-mirrors`, with no test or baseline edited |\n131:| REQ-003 | A request for a named hook's README, such as \"README for the session-handover hook\", and one for a runtime folder's README still top sk-doc |\n132:| REQ-004 | The holdout returns to 49 of 63 or more and `rr-iter3-069` returns to its ledger top, both by narrowing a phrase main added |\n133:| REQ-005 | `skill-graph-freshness.cjs --strict` exits 0 and `generate-router-intent-signals.cjs --check` passes |\n134:| REQ-006 | Review pass ten's two P1 are fixed: a single-quoted command name reads like a plain one before its refusal or question lead, and the doctor install presentation, workflow and contract test agree on the runtimes the link manifest offers |\n156:| Risk | A narrower phrase stops a named hook README request reaching sk-doc | Medium | REQ-003 checks named hook and runtime folder README prompts through the advisor CLI |\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"45:- Main's commits `fad83abd791` (root g