s (try-variant.sh no-git-named+names:spec-gate)\ntasks.md:46:- [x] T003 Narrow the runtime folder and hook mirror README phrases (`$DOC/ROUTER.md`, `$DOC/sk-create-readme/ROUTER.md`). Verify: slice row doctor-a-10 passes. Evidence: \"hook mirror readme\" dropped from RUNTIME_PLUGIN_README (7 to 6); doctor-a-10 passes; sk-create-readme/ROUTER.md carries no advisor intent, left as is\ntasks.md:56:- [x] T006 [C] Probe README requests through the advisor CLI (`$SP/readme-probes.txt`). After T005. Verify: the session-handover hook, git-preflight hook and runtime folder README requests each top sk-doc. Evidence: readme-probes.txt: session-handover, git-preflight and spec-gate hook READMEs, runtime and plugins folder READMEs and SECURITY.md top sk-doc; git hooks, git rules, git standards top sk-git; runtime mirror drift tops command-doctor-runtime-mirrors\ntasks.md:60:- [x] T010 [C] Fix review pass ten's single-quoted command P1 (`$ADV/lib/command-attach.ts`, `$ADV/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts`). Verify: the quote cases fail without the fix. Evidence: a single quote is dropped only where it opens a command name; three cases fail without it, 167 pass with it; contractions keep their apostrophe\ntasks.md:61:- [x] T011 [C] Fix review pass ten's doctor install P1 (`.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-install-presentation.txt`, `doctor-install.yaml`, `scripts/tests/doctor-install-contract.test.cjs`). Verify: the contract passes and fails with main's wording. Evidence: the presentation names claude, codex, cursor, devin, dsh, opencode, pi and vibe from the manifest; the stale DSH sentence is gone from the workflow; the test reads the manifest; 17/17, and 16/1 with main's text; doctor tests 1266/0\ntasks.md:62:- [x] T012 [C] Rerun the gates after the pass ten fixes (`$SP/after-pass-ten.txt`). Verify: 0 failed both ways. Evidence: 2353 passed 0 failed with the flag unset and set, FLOOR 24/44 0/35 2/44, EVAL [160,49,21,5], stored sets unchanged; one doctor case failed only while the advisor dist rebuilt in parallel and passes 1266/0 on rerun\ntasks.md:113:- [x] CHK-011 [P1] No test, baseline or ledger file changed. Evidence: no test, baseline or ledger file changed for the routing repair; the doctor contract test changed only for the pass-ten P1\ntasks.md:132:- [x] CHK-FIX-001 [P0] Each fix names its class. Evidence: data fix at the producer for the routing; producer fix for the quote; merge drift for the doctor wording\nacceptance-criteria.md:55:| AC-002 | REQ-002 | Given \"git hooks\", \"git rules\", \"git standards\", \"git hooks broken\" and \"runtime mirror drift\", When `doctor-bridge-isolation` and `doctor-routing-slice` run, Then each passes with no test or baseline file changed | both test files pass in `scratch/after.txt`; `git diff --stat` lists no test or baseline file | Met | - |\nacceptance-criteria.md:59:| AC-006 | REQ-006 | Given `do not run '/create:readme' yet` and the doctor install files, When the guards test and `doctor-install-contract.test.cjs` run, Then the quoted refusal reads as a mention and the contract passes, and both fail without the fix | three quote cases fail without the fix and 167 pass with it; the contract passes 17/17 and fails with main's text; doctor tests 1266/0 | Met | - |\nimplementation-summary.md:48:Bare git prompts, the runtime mirror doctor and two scorer gates route as they did before the merge again. The sk-doc README intents main added had given sk-doc words that other skills own. Those phrases are now narrower, and README requests still reach their templates.\nimplementation-summary.md:52:You can ask for \"git hooks\", \"git rules\" or \"git standards\" and reach sk-git again, and \"runtime mirror drift\" reaches `/doctor:runtime-mirrors`. A request for a named hook's README, a runtime or plugins folder README or a `SECURITY.md` still lands on sk-doc. The compiled skill graph matches its sources again, so the strict freshness check passes.\nimplementation-summary.md:62:| `runtime/