{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794852322710,"sessionID":"ses_e1a82d918ffeSg4o2dc6d2Zt3H","part":{"partID":"prt_1e588f9de001TxkOmky4N51hEN","sessionID":"ses_e1a82d918ffeSg4o2dc6d2Zt3H","messageID":"msg_1e588d459001pxqKROtEw69qLH","type":"tool","id":"call_cac562fa82d7417f80a4c8df","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/039-main-sk-doc-routing-repair && sed -n '50,70p' acceptance-criteria.md; echo \"===CHK===\"; sed -n '120,140p' tasks.md; echo \"===IMPL===\"; sed -n '40,75p' implementation-summary.md"},"output":"One row per criterion. `AC-ID` is stable once written: supersede a criterion, never renumber it. A new row takes the highest AC-ID plus one.\n\n| AC-ID | REQ | Given / When / Then | Verification | Status | Waiver |\n|-------|-----|---------------------|--------------|--------|--------|\n| AC-001 | REQ-001 | Given the narrowed phrases, When the advisor suite runs with `AI_SESSION_CHILD` unset and set to 1 and `FLOOR` runs, Then 0 failed both ways and `FLOOR` prints 24/44, 0/35 and 2/44 | `scratch/after-pass-ten.txt`: 2353 passed 0 failed with the flag unset and set; FLOOR 24/44, 0/35, 2/44 | Met | - |\n| AC-002 | REQ-002 | Given \"git hooks\", \"git rules\", \"git standards\", \"git hooks broken\" and \"runtime mirror drift\", When `doctor-bridge-isolation` and `doctor-routing-slice` run, Then each passes with no test or baseline file changed | both test files pass in `scratch/after.txt`; `git diff --stat` lists no test or baseline file | Met | - |\n| AC-003 | REQ-003 | Given README requests for the session-handover hook, the git-preflight hook and a runtime folder, When the advisor CLI scores them, Then each tops sk-doc | `scratch/readme-probes.txt` | Met | - |\n| AC-004 | REQ-004 | Given the independent holdout and the ratchet ledger, When their tests run, Then the holdout prints 49 of 63 or more and `rr-iter3-069` matches its ledger top, with no baseline or ledger edit | both test files pass; no baseline or ledger file changed | Met | - |\n| AC-005 | REQ-005 | Given the regenerated intent signals and the recompiled graph, When `generate-router-intent-signals.cjs --check` and `skill-graph-freshness.cjs --strict` run, Then both exit 0 | `scratch/after.txt`: RESULT: PASSED and graph freshness exit 0 | Met | - |\n| AC-006 | REQ-006 | Given `do not run '/create:readme' yet` and the doctor install files, When the guards test and `doctor-install-contract.test.cjs` run, Then the quoted refusal reads as a mention and the contract passes, and both fail without the fix | three quote cases fail without the fix and 167 pass with it; the contract passes 17/17 and fails with main's text; doctor tests 1266/0 | Met | - |\n\n### Status values\n\n| Value | Meaning |\n|-------|---------|\n| `Met` | Verified. The Verification cell names evidence that was actually observed. |\n| `Unmet` | Not yet satisfied. Blocks closure. |\n| `Waived` | Deliberately not pursued. Requires an ADR in the Waiver cell. |\n| `Superseded` | Replaced by a different criterion or decision. Requires an ADR in the Waiver cell. |\n\n### Waiver cell\n===CHK===\n\n- [x] CHK-020 [P0] All acceptance criteria met. Evidence: acceptance-criteria all Met\n- [x] CHK-021 [P0] Full suite 0 failed with the flag unset and set (`after.txt`). Evidence: after-pass-ten.txt 2353/0 both ways\n- [x] CHK-022 [P1] README requests still reach sk-doc (`readme-probes.txt`). Evidence: readme-probes.txt\n- [x] CHK-023 [P1] `FLOOR` unchanged and `EVAL` not lower. Evidence: FLOOR and EVAL equal before.txt\n<!-- /ANCHOR:testing -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:fix-completeness -->\n## FIX ADDENDUM: FIX COMPLETENESS\n\n- [x] CHK-FIX-001 [P0] Each fix names its class. Evidence: data fix at the producer for the routing; producer fix for the quote; merge drift for the doctor wording\n- [x] CHK-FIX-002 [P0] Every README intent main added was checked for the same class. Evidence: every README intent main added was measured in try-variant.sh\n<!-- /ANCHOR:fix-completeness -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:security -->\n## Security\n\n===IMPL===\n| **Level** | 2 |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:metadata -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:what-built -->\n## What Was Built\n\nBare git prompts, the runtime mirror doctor and two scorer gates route as they did before the merge again. The sk-doc README intents main added had given sk-doc words that other skills own. Those phrases are now narrower, and README requests still reach their templates.\n\n### Phase 39: main-sk-doc-routing-repair\n\nYou can ask for \"git hooks\", \"git rules\" or \"git standards\" and reach sk-git again, and \"runtime mirror drift\" reaches `/doctor:runtime-mirrors`. A request for a named hook's README, a runtime or plugins folder README or a `SECURITY.md` still lands on sk-doc. The compiled skill graph matches its sources again, so the strict freshness check passes.\n\n### Files Changed\n\n| File | Action | Purpose |\n|------|--------|---------|\n| `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/ROUTER.md` | Modified | The `HOOK_README` intent drops the `git-*` and `spec-gate` named phrases, `RUNTIME_PLUGIN_README` drops \"hook mirror readme\", `SECURITY_POLICY` keeps \"security.md\" only, and the prose says why |\n| `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/graph-metadata.json` | Modified | Intent signals regenerated from the router |\n| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/skill-graph.json` | Modified | Recompiled graph |\n| `scratch/try-variant.py`, `scratch/try-variant.sh` | Created | Measure one keyword variant against the failing tests |\n| `runtime/lib/command-attach.ts` and its guards test | Modified | A single quote that opens a command name is dropped before the lead reading, from review pass ten |\n| Doctor install presentation, workflow and contract test | Modified | Name the eight manifest runtimes and drop the stale DSH sentence, from review pass ten |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:what-built -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:how-delivered -->\n## How It Was Delivered\n\nEach candidate change was applied to a clean router, regenerated and measured against the five failing test files by `scratch/try-variant.sh`. Main's new intents were removed one at a time to find which moved the holdout count and the ratchet row, so no holdout row was read. The chosen variant then ran the full gate both ways, and the README probes went through the advisor CLI.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:how-delivered -->\n\n---\n\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"One row per criterion. `AC-ID` is stable once written: supersede a criterion, never renumber it. A new row takes the highest AC-ID plus one.\n\n| AC-ID | REQ | Given / When / Then | Verification | Status | Waiver |\n|-------|-----|---------------------|--------------|--------|--------|\n| AC-001 | REQ-001 | Given the narrowed phrases, When the advisor suite runs with `AI_SESSION_CHILD` unset and set to 1 and `FLOOR` runs, Then 0 failed both ways and `FLOOR` prints 24/44, 0/35 and 2/44 | `scratch/after-pass-ten.txt`: 2353 passed 0 failed with the flag unset and set; FLOOR 24/44, 0/35, 2/44 | Met | - |\n| AC-002 | REQ-002 | Given \"git hooks\", \"git rules\", \"git standards\", \"git hooks broken\" and \"runtime mirror drift\", When `doctor-bridge-isolation` and `doctor-routing-slice` run, Then each passes with no test or baseline file changed | both test files pass in `scratch/after.txt`; `git diff --stat` lists no test or baseline file | Met | - |\n| AC-003 | REQ-003 | Given README requests for the session-handover hook, the git-preflight hook and a runtime folder, When the advisor CLI scores them, Then each tops sk-doc | `scratch/readme-probes.txt` | Met | - |\n| AC-004 | REQ-004 | Given the independent holdout and the ratchet ledger, When their tests run, Then the holdout prints 49 of 63 or more and `rr-iter3-069` matches its ledger top, with no baseline or ledger edit | both test files pass; no baseline or ledger file changed | Met | - |\n| AC-005 | REQ-005 | Given the regenerated intent signals and the recompiled graph, When `generate-router-intent-signals.cjs --check` and `skill-graph-freshness.cjs --strict` run, Then both exit 0 | `scratch/after.txt`: RESULT: PASSED and graph freshness exit 0 | Met | - |\n| AC-006 | REQ-006 | Given `do not run '/create:readme' yet` and the doctor install files, When the guards test and `doctor-install-contract.test.cjs` run, Then the quoted refusal reads as a mention and the contract passes, and both fail without the fix | three quote cases fail without the fix and 167 pass with it; the contract passes 17/17 and fails with main's text; doctor tests 1266/0 | Met | - |\n\n### Status values\n\n| Value | Meaning |\n|-------|---------|\n| `Met` | Verified. The Verification cell names evidence that was actually observed. |\n| `Unmet` | Not yet satisfied. Blocks closure. |\n| `Waived` | Deliberately not pursued. Requires an ADR in the Waiver cell. |\n| `Superseded` | Replaced by a different criterion or decision. Requires an ADR in the Waiver cell. |\n\n### Waiver cell\n===CHK===\n\n- [x] CHK-020 [P0] All acceptance criteria met. Evidence: acceptance-criteria all Met\n- [x] CHK-021 [P0] Full suite 0 failed with the flag unset and set (`after.txt`). Evidence: after-pass-ten.txt 2353/0 both ways\n- [x] CHK-022 [P1] README requests still reach sk-doc (`readme-probes.txt`). Evidence: readme-probes.txt\n- [x] CHK-023 [P1] `FLOOR` unchanged and `EVAL` not lower. Evidence: FLOOR and EVAL equal before.txt\n<!-- /ANCHOR:testing -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:fix-completeness -->\n## FIX ADDENDUM: FIX COMPLETENESS\n\n- [x] CHK-FIX-001 [P0] Each fix names its class. Evidence: data fix at the producer for the routing; producer fix for the quote; merge drift for the doctor wording\n- [x] CHK-FIX-002 [P0] Every README intent main added was checked for the same class. Evidence: every README intent main added was measured in try-variant.sh\n<!-- /ANCHOR:fix-completeness -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:security -->\n## Security\n\n===IMPL===\n| **Level** | 2 |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:metadata -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:what-built -->\n## What Was Built\n\nBare git prompts, the runtime mirror doctor and two scorer gates route as they did before the merge again. The sk-doc README intents main added had given sk-doc words that other skills own. Those phrases are now narrower, and README requests still reach their templates.\n\n### Phase 39: main-sk-doc-routing-repair\n\nYou can ask for \"git hooks\", \"git rules\" or \"git standards\" and reach sk-git again, and \"runtime mirror drift\" reaches `/doctor:runtime-mirrors`. A request for a named hook's README, a runtime or plugins folder README or a `SECURITY.md` still lands on sk-doc. The compiled skill graph matches its sources again, so the strict freshness check passes.\n\n### Files Changed\n\n| File | Action | Purpose |\n|------|--------|---------|\n| `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/ROUTER.md` | Modified | The `HOOK_README` intent drops the `git-*` and `spec-gate` named phrases, `RUNTIME_PLUGIN_README` drops \"hook mirror readme\", `SECURITY_POLICY` keeps \"security.md\" only, and the prose says why |\n| `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/graph-metadata.json` | Modified | Intent signals regenerated from the router |\n| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/skill-graph.json` | Modified | Recompiled graph |\n| `scratch/try-variant.py`, `scratch/try-variant.sh` | Created | Measure one keyword variant against the failing tests |\n| `runtime/lib/command-attach.ts` and its guards test | Modified | A single quote that opens a command name is dropped before the lead reading, from review pass ten |\n| Doctor install presentation, workflow and contract test | Modified | Name the eight manifest runtimes and drop the stale DSH sentence, from review pass ten |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:what-built -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:how-delivered -->\n## How It Was Delivered\n\nEach candidate change was applied to a clean router, regenerated and measured against the five failing test files by `scratch/try-variant.sh`. Main's new intents were removed one at a time to find which moved the holdout count and the ratchet row, so no holdout row was read. The chosen variant then ran the full gate both ways, and the README probes went through the advisor CLI.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:how-delivered -->\n\n---\n\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/039-main-sk-doc-routing-repair && sed -n '50,70p' acceptance-criteria.md; echo \\\"===CHK===\\\"; sed -n '120,140p' tasks.md; echo \\\"===IMPL===\\\"; sed -n '40,75p' implementation-summary.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794852321758,"end":1794852322710}}}}
