{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794852344837,"sessionID":"ses_e1a82d918ffeSg4o2dc6d2Zt3H","part":{"partID":"prt_1e5894ed8002kN7cMEjsS75BCg","sessionID":"ses_e1a82d918ffeSg4o2dc6d2Zt3H","messageID":"msg_1e58902a60014Ho2vULM2TWLpO","type":"tool","id":"call_82957de83b084f98bb1f3c7b","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && grep -rn \"claude,opencode,codex\\|claude, codex, cursor, devin, dsh\" .skilled/commands/doctor .skilled/skills/system-skilled-doctor 2>/dev/null | grep -v tests | head -10; echo \"===FEATURE CATALOG===\"; grep -rln \"doctor:install\" .skilled/skills/*/feature-catalog* .skilled/skills/*/*feature-catalog* 2>/dev/null | head -5"},"output":".skilled/commands/doctor/install.md:37:- `--root <dir>` is the target repo's absolute path. `--runtimes <list>` is a comma list drawn from `claude,opencode,codex,cursor,devin,pi,vibe,dsh`; without it the engine keeps the runtimes its own detection finds in the root. `--json` prints one JSON object and nothing else.\n.skilled/commands/doctor/symlink.md:57:| `--runtimes <list>` | `check`, `link` | Link only these runtimes, from `claude,opencode,codex,cursor,devin,pi,vibe,dsh`. `.skilled` is always included |\n.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-symlink-link.yaml:52:  runtimes: \"Optional comma-separated runtime names: claude,opencode,codex,cursor,devin,pi,vibe,dsh. When omitted, the engine selects runtimes whose primary entry already exists in the target root. The core entry is always included.\"\n.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-symlink-check.yaml:45:  runtimes: \"Optional comma-separated runtime names, passed as --runtimes <list> when supplied: claude,opencode,codex,cursor,devin,pi,vibe,dsh. When omitted, the engine selects runtimes whose primary entry already exists in the target root. The core entry is always included.\"\n.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-install-presentation.txt:78:A runtime name outside claude, codex, cursor, devin, dsh, opencode, pi and vibe or the ones already there, a shape outside the three, or an instruction word outside the two is not guessed. Ask that one question again with the accepted values. When the engine refuses a root, show its `ERROR:` line as it printed and ask question 1 again.\n===FEATURE CATALOG===\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/feature-catalog/doctor-commands/category-overview.md\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/feature-catalog/doctor-commands/category-overview.md\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":".skilled/commands/doctor/install.md:37:- `--root <dir>` is the target repo's absolute path. `--runtimes <list>` is a comma list drawn from `claude,opencode,codex,cursor,devin,pi,vibe,dsh`; without it the engine keeps the runtimes its own detection finds in the root. `--json` prints one JSON object and nothing else.\n.skilled/commands/doctor/symlink.md:57:| `--runtimes <list>` | `check`, `link` | Link only these runtimes, from `claude,opencode,codex,cursor,devin,pi,vibe,dsh`. `.skilled` is always included |\n.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-symlink-link.yaml:52:  runtimes: \"Optional comma-separated runtime names: claude,opencode,codex,cursor,devin,pi,vibe,dsh. When omitted, the engine selects runtimes whose primary entry already exists in the target root. The core entry is always included.\"\n.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-symlink-check.yaml:45:  runtimes: \"Optional comma-separated runtime names, passed as --runtimes <list> when supplied: claude,opencode,codex,cursor,devin,pi,vibe,dsh. When omitted, the engine selects runtimes whose primary entry already exists in the target root. The core entry is always included.\"\n.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-install-presentation.txt:78:A runtime name outside claude, codex, cursor, devin, dsh, opencode, pi and vibe or the ones already there, a shape outside the three, or an instruction word outside the two is not guessed. Ask that one question again with the accepted values. When the engine refuses a root, show its `ERROR:` line as it printed and ask question 1 again.\n===FEATURE CATALOG===\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/feature-catalog/doctor-commands/category-overview.md\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/feature-catalog/doctor-commands/category-overview.md\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && grep -rn \\\"claude,opencode,codex\\\\|claude, codex, cursor, devin, dsh\\\" .skilled/commands/doctor .skilled/skills/system-skilled-doctor 2>/dev/null | grep -v tests | head -10; echo \\\"===FEATURE CATALOG===\\\"; grep -rln \\\"doctor:install\\\" .skilled/skills/*/feature-catalog* .skilled/skills/*/*feature-catalog* 2>/dev/null | head -5\"}"},"time":{"start":1794852343512,"end":1794852344837}}}}
