{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794852350421,"sessionID":"ses_e1a82d918ffeSg4o2dc6d2Zt3H","part":{"partID":"prt_1e589671c001kY4peHH6xAx0e1","sessionID":"ses_e1a82d918ffeSg4o2dc6d2Zt3H","messageID":"msg_1e5895831001n1G6OnSRZRr463","type":"tool","id":"call_3c873cca9aee48f2a873d476","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && grep -n \"install\\|runtimes\\|nine\\|eight\" .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/feature-catalog/doctor-commands/category-overview.md | head -20"},"output":"17:Category covering the doctor routers split by owner: `/doctor:speckit` for spec-kit retrieval, `/doctor:skill-advisor <target>` with six targets, `/doctor:deep-loop` and `/doctor:runtime-mirrors`, `/doctor:ci <report|scaffold|toggle>` for GitHub Actions workflows, `/doctor:sk-skill <check|convert>` for skill format work, `/doctor:agents-md <check|embed|restore>` for the root instruction file, plus `/doctor:helper`, which names the command that fits a described problem, `/doctor:setup`, the read-only onboarding check across all of them, and standalone `/doctor:update`, `/doctor:mcp install|debug`, `/doctor:env`, `/doctor:sk-code` and `/doctor:git <hooks|standards|setup>` commands.\n25:The shipped surface splits by owner. `/doctor:speckit` takes no target and diagnoses spec-kit retrieval: the trigger index, its lookup and the ripgrep recipes. `/doctor:skill-advisor <target>` owns six targets: `tune`, `rebuild`, `skill-graph-freshness`, `router-reach`, `skill-budget` and `parent-skill`. The `rebuild` target rebuilds `skill-graph.sqlite` through the advisor CLI behind a backup. `/doctor:deep-loop` takes only `--scope`, and `/doctor:runtime-mirrors` takes no arguments. `/doctor:setup` takes no target: it lists every doctor command and runs the sk-code setup, sk-git setup, trigger index, runtime mirror and skill advisor status checks read-only, naming one repair command per failing check. Standalone `/doctor:update` carries check, align, gated apply, rollback, record-base and compat actions and owns release migration. `/doctor:mcp install|debug`, `/doctor:env`, `/doctor:sk-code` and `/doctor:git <hooks|standards|setup>` complete the set. `/doctor:ci` owns three targets. `report` (the default, read-only) lists every GitHub Actions workflow with its switch state. `scaffold` writes one new workflow after a yes. `toggle` changes one switch variable after a yes, but it refuses to switch off the master or message-contract switch.\n29:`/doctor:agents-md <check|embed|restore>` answers the same question for the root instruction file. `check` is the default and read-only: it reports twelve rows from the shipped manifest, covering the install state, the sections lost or reordered, how current each shipped body is, every pin, the delivery budget, the shape of the repository block, the lines only the repository carries, each runtime copy, the `REPO RULES.md` router and the template's own purity, and it reads `UNKNOWN` rather than `PASS` for a row it cannot prove. `embed` composes every target in memory, prints the targets, the diffs, the new block, the budget, the preservation ledger and a plan digest, and writes only when that digest comes back: it backs up every path it will touch, writes inside its own allowlist and proves against the bytes on disk that no repository line was dropped, restoring from the backup itself when one was. `restore` puts back exactly the paths one recorded run's `manifest.json` names. A repository already in its target state gets `NOTHING TO DO`, and no route stages or commits anything.\n50:| `.skilled/commands/doctor/install.md` | Router | `/doctor:install` read-only guide that checks the two builds, runs the symlink check and prints the ordered setup commands |\n58:| `.skilled/commands/doctor/mcp.md` | Command | `/doctor:mcp install\\|debug` MCP infra surface |\n73:| `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/agents-md-check.test.cjs` | Validator | The check engine over the nine composed fixture recipes: the state each one plants, the row it must fail, the exit codes, JSON parity and the tree digests |\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"17:Category covering the doctor routers split by owner: `/doctor:speckit` for spec-kit retrieval, `/doctor:skill-advisor <target>` with six targets, `/doctor:deep-loop` and `/doctor:runtime-mirrors`, `/doctor:ci <report|scaffold|toggle>` for GitHub Actions workflows, `/doctor:sk-skill <check|convert>` for skill format work, `/doctor:agents-md <check|embed|restore>` for the root instruction file, plus `/doctor:helper`, which names the command that fits a described problem, `/doctor:setup`, the read-only onboarding check across all of them, and standalone `/doctor:update`, `/doctor:mcp install|debug`, `/doctor:env`, `/doctor:sk-code` and `/doctor:git <hooks|standards|setup>` commands.\n25:The shipped surface splits by owner. `/doctor:speckit` takes no target and diagnoses spec-kit retrieval: the trigger index, its lookup and the ripgrep recipes. `/doctor:skill-advisor <target>` owns six targets: `tune`, `rebuild`, `skill-graph-freshness`, `router-reach`, `skill-budget` and `parent-skill`. The `rebuild` target rebuilds `skill-graph.sqlite` through the advisor CLI behind a backup. `/doctor:deep-loop` takes only `--scope`, and `/doctor:runtime-mirrors` takes no arguments. `/doctor:setup` takes no target: it lists every doctor command and runs the sk-code setup, sk-git setup, trigger index, runtime mirror and skill advisor status checks read-only, naming one repair command per failing check. Standalone `/doctor:update` carries check, align, gated apply, rollback, record-base and compat actions and owns release migration. `/doctor:mcp install|debug`, `/doctor:env`, `/doctor:sk-code` and `/doctor:git <hooks|standards|setup>` complete the set. `/doctor:ci` owns three targets. `report` (the default, read-only) lists every GitHub Actions workflow with its switch state. `scaffold` writes one new workflow after a yes. `toggle` changes one switch variable after a yes, but it refuses to switch off the master or message-contract switch.\n29:`/doctor:agents-md <check|embed|restore>` answers the same question for the root instruction file. `check` is the default and read-only: it reports twelve rows from the shipped manifest, covering the install state, the sections lost or reordered, how current each shipped body is, every pin, the delivery budget, the shape of the repository block, the lines only the repository carries, each runtime copy, the `REPO RULES.md` router and the template's own purity, and it reads `UNKNOWN` rather than `PASS` for a row it cannot prove. `embed` composes every target in memory, prints the targets, the diffs, the new block, the budget, the preservation ledger and a plan digest, and writes only when that digest comes back: it backs up every path it will touch, writes inside its own allowlist and proves against the bytes on disk that no repository line was dropped, restoring from the backup itself when one was. `restore` puts back exactly the paths one recorded run's `manifest.json` names. A repository already in its target state gets `NOTHING TO DO`, and no route stages or commits anything.\n50:| `.skilled/commands/doctor/install.md` | Router | `/doctor:install` read-only guide that checks the two builds, runs the symlink check and prints the ordered setup commands |\n58:| `.skilled/commands/doctor/mcp.md` | Command | `/doctor:mcp install\\|debug` MCP infra surface |\n73:| `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/agents-md-check.test.cjs` | Validator | The check engine over the nine composed fixture recipes: the state each one plants, the row it must fail, the exit codes, JSON parity and the tree digests |\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && grep -n \\\"install\\\\|runtimes\\\\|nine\\\\|eight\\\" .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/feature-catalog/doctor-commands/category-overview.md | head -20\"}"},"time":{"start":1794852349724,"end":1794852350421}}}}
{"type":"step_finish","timestamp":1794852351615,"sessionID":"ses_e1a82d918ffeSg4o2dc6d2Zt3H","part":{"id":"prt_1e5896e7f001705qeoe0hprwcy","sessionID":"ses_e1a82d918ffeSg4o2dc6d2Zt3H","messageID":"msg_1e5895831001n1G6OnSRZRr463","type":"step-finish","reason":"tool-calls","snapshot":"dec0594770792fd4c9a06476e88141852dc0da1f","cost":0,"tokens":{"input":2205,"output":102,"reasoning":30,"cache":{"read":160896,"write":0}}}}
