{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794852362447,"sessionID":"ses_e1a82d918ffeSg4o2dc6d2Zt3H","part":{"partID":"prt_1e58996ac001RgicZwsT6ZGqla","sessionID":"ses_e1a82d918ffeSg4o2dc6d2Zt3H","messageID":"msg_1e5896e86001vo8xpIetPGe436","type":"tool","id":"call_067e7ddde31343e9a0d186f4","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && grep -n \"doctor:install\" -A 40 .skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml | head -60"},"output":"22:#   /doctor:install         .skilled/commands/doctor/install.md\n23-#   /doctor:overlay         .skilled/commands/doctor/overlay.md\n24-# A command that owns one route needs no positional target.\n25-# Validated by: .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/route-validate.sh\n26-# Consumed by: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/derive-command-bridges.cjs\n27-#   turns every route, every standalone command and every mcp_subroutes\n28-#   entry into one advisor command bridge, copies its trigger_phrases into\n29-#   the TypeScript scorer and its runnable command into the Python slash\n30-#   markers and the brief's lookup. A bridge routes only once\n31-#   scoring-compatibility.json beside the deriver activates it. Doctor\n32-#   dispatch itself stays argv-driven (see each router).\n33-#\n34-# Schema (per route):\n35-#   command:          string — the doctor command that owns the route\n36-#   target:           string — positional name the user types\n37-#   yaml:             string — YAML asset filename in assets/\n38-#   setup_vars:       list   — variables the router resolves and passes to YAML\n39-#   allowed_flags:    list   — per-target flag schema (target-first parsing)\n40-#   mutating:         enum   — read-only | add-only | mutates\n41-#   gate3_location:   string — concrete mutation target (or \"n/a\" for read-only)\n42-#   write_scope:      enum   — optional; spec-folder marks an add-only route whose every write lands in the bound spec folder\n43-#   mcp_tools:        list   — subset of router's frontmatter allowed-tools union\n44-#   trigger_phrases:  list   — diagnostic routing phrases for this target, three or\n45-#                              more words each; the bridge deriver copies them\n46-#                              into the advisor (see \"Consumed by\" above)\n47-#   default_target:   bool   — optional; true marks the read-only target a bare typed command\n48-#                              should suggest (the router's no-token target, or its read-only\n49-#                              entry point), so /doctor:ci alone also reaches this route's\n50-#                              advisor bridge. At most one per command, only on a command with\n51-#                              several targets, and never on a mutating route.\n52-#   lead_phrases:     list   — optional subset of trigger_phrases that puts this bridge ahead of a passing skill when the prompt contains the phrase. Use it only where the doctor command must lead the skill.\n53-#\n54-# Skill-advisor recommendation tools are registered through system-skill-advisor.\n55-# To add a new target:\n56-#   1. Append the route here with its owning command and trigger_phrases of three or more words. Add lead_phrases only for a phrase where the doctor command must rank above a passing skill.\n57-#   2. List the target in that command's router and presentation, and add its row to the /doctor:setup target list in .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup-presentation.txt.\n58-#   3. To let the advisor suggest it, add its activation entry to both the \"typescript\" and \"python\" lists in .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/scoring-compatibility.json. A bridge without one stays inactive.\n59-#   4. Rerun node .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/derive-command-bridges.cjs, then bash .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/route-validate.sh and node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/doctor-phrase-reach.cjs.\n60-#   5. /doctor:helper needs no edit: it ranks this manifest at run time, and its contract test fails until the new route is reachable and listed in the /doctor:setup target list.\n61-# To remove a target: delete the route AND its corresponding assets/doctor-<target>.yaml.\n62-# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n--\n636:  - command: /doctor:install\n637-    target: guide\n638-    yaml: doctor-install.yaml\n639-    setup_vars: [execution_mode, root, runtimes, json_output]\n640-    allowed_flags: [\"--json\", \"--root <dir>\", \"--runtimes <list>\"]\n641-    mutating: read-only\n642-    gate3_location: \"n/a (read-only guide; it checks the two builds, runs the symlink engine's check once and prints the ordered writing commands for the operator to run)\"\n643-    mcp_tools: []   # script-only; no MCP calls\n644-    script_invocations:\n645-      - 'test -d .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/dist  # the spec-kit build the session hooks load'\n646-      - 'node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs list-tools --format json  # the advisor build; exit 0 means built'\n647-      - 'node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/symlink-engine.cjs check --root <dir>  # the workflow adds --runtimes and --link-instructions only when the operator chose them'\n648-    trigger_phrases:\n649-      - \"install skilled into my project\"\n650-      - \"set up skilled in another repo\"\n651-      - \"use skilled in my own project\"\n652-      - \"onboard a project repo to skilled\"\n653-      - \"guide me through installing skilled\"\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"22:#   /doctor:install         .skilled/commands/doctor/install.md\n23-#   /doctor:overlay         .skilled/commands/doctor/overlay.md\n24-# A command that owns one route needs no positional target.\n25-# Validated by: .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/route-validate.sh\n26-# Consumed by: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/derive-command-bridges.cjs\n27-#   turns every route, every standalone command and every mcp_subroutes\n28-#   entry into one advisor command bridge, copies its trigger_phrases into\n29-#   the TypeScript scorer and its runnable command into the Python slash\n30-#   markers and the brief's lookup. A bridge routes only once\n31-#   scoring-compatibility.json beside the deriver activates it. Doctor\n32-#   dispatch itself stays argv-driven (see each router).\n33-#\n34-# Schema (per route):\n35-#   command:          string — the doctor command that owns the route\n36-#   target:           string — positional name the user types\n37-#   yaml:             string — YAML asset filename in assets/\n38-#   setup_vars:       list   — variables the router resolves and passes to YAML\n39-#   allowed_flags:    list   — per-target flag schema (target-first parsing)\n40-#   mutating:         enum   — read-only | add-only | mutates\n41-#   gate3_location:   string — concrete mutation target (or \"n/a\" for read-only)\n42-#   write_scope:      enum   — optional; spec-folder marks an add-only route whose every write lands in the bound spec folder\n43-#   mcp_tools:        list   — subset of router's frontmatter allowed-tools union\n44-#   trigger_phrases:  list   — diagnostic routing phrases for this target, three or\n45-#                              more words each; the bridge deriver copies them\n46-#                              into the advisor (see \"Consumed by\" above)\n47-#   default_target:   bool   — optional; true marks the read-only target a bare typed command\n48-#                              should suggest (the router's no-token target, or its read-only\n49-#                              entry point), so /doctor:ci alone also reaches this route's\n50-#                              advisor bridge. At most one per command, only on a command with\n51-#                              several targets, and never on a mutating route.\n52-#   lead_phrases:     list   — optional subset of trigger_phrases that puts this bridge ahead of a passing skill when the prompt contains the phrase. Use it only where the doctor command must lead the skill.\n53-#\n54-# Skill-advisor recommendation tools are registered through system-skill-advisor.\n55-# To add a new target:\n56-#   1. Append the route here with its owning command and trigger_phrases of three or more words. Add lead_phrases only for a phrase where the doctor command must rank above a passing skill.\n57-#   2. List the target in that command's router and presentation, and add its row to the /doctor:setup target list in .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup-presentation.txt.\n58-#   3. To let the advisor suggest it, add its activation entry to both the \"typescript\" and \"python\" lists in .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/scoring-compatibility.json. A bridge without one stays inactive.\n59-#   4. Rerun node .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/derive-command-bridges.cjs, then bash .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/route-validate.sh and node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/doctor-phrase-reach.cjs.\n60-#   5. /doctor:helper needs no edit: it ranks this manifest at run time, and its contract test fails until the new route is reachable and listed in the /doctor:setup target list.\n61-# To remove a target: delete the route AND its corresponding assets/doctor-<target>.yaml.\n62-# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n--\n636:  - command: /doctor:install\n637-    target: guide\n638-    yaml: doctor-install.yaml\n639-    setup_vars: [execution_mode, root, runtimes, json_output]\n640-    allowed_flags: [\"--json\", \"--root <dir>\", \"--runtimes <list>\"]\n641-    mutating: read-only\n642-    gate3_location: \"n/a (read-only guide; it checks the two builds, runs the symlink engine's check once and prints the ordered writing commands for the operator to run)\"\n643-    mcp_tools: []   # script-only; no MCP calls\n644-    script_invocations:\n645-      - 'test -d .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/dist  # the spec-kit build the session hooks load'\n646-      - 'node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs list-tools --format json  # the advisor build; exit 0 means built'\n647-      - 'node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/symlink-engine.cjs check --root <dir>  # the workflow adds --runtimes and --link-instructions only when the operator chose them'\n648-    trigger_phrases:\n649-      - \"install skilled into my project\"\n650-      - \"set up skilled in another repo\"\n651-      - \"use skilled in my own project\"\n652-      - \"onboard a project repo to skilled\"\n653-      - \"guide me through installing skilled\"\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && grep -n \\\"doctor:install\\\" -A 40 .skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml | head -60\"}"},"time":{"start":1794852361900,"end":1794852362447}}}}
