{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794852706416,"sessionID":"ses_e1a82d918ffeSg4o2dc6d2Zt3H","part":{"partID":"prt_1e58ed5c6001gsH0b2siPtIU85","sessionID":"ses_e1a82d918ffeSg4o2dc6d2Zt3H","messageID":"msg_1e58ec6f40012BgFZC5KlcYj8O","type":"tool","id":"call_c121c81c9daa40c4b15cc720","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && grep -n \"ANCHOR:next-focus\" -A 12 specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/fixes-11/deep-review-strategy.md"},"output":"139:<!-- ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n140-## 11. NEXT FOCUS\n141-- **Dimension:** security. - **Focus area:** whether the mention guard can be evaded by quote placement to make the advisor offer or deliver a command the prompt refused, and whether the doctor install's printed writing commands can carry operator input beyond the values it validated. - **Reason:** the guard's purpose is to keep a mutating command from being offered on a refusal; iteration 1 found one reachable evasion, so the adversarial pass should map the family rather than add a second instance of it. - **Rotation status:** correctness and traceability reviewed; security next, maintainability last. - **Blocked/productive carry-forward:** traceability is productive (two P2s, both with a concrete mutation that keeps tests green); no approach is blocked. - **Required evidence:** compiled-module runs over quote/lead permutations (brace, quote, apostrophe, list joins), and the presentation's printed-command invariants at `doctor-install-presentation.txt:5` and `:139`. **Stop decision after iteration 1:** CONTINUE; `stopReason` none; `blockedBy` empty; the coverage gate names `security`, `traceability` and `maintainability` as the missing dimensions at that point, and `traceability` is now covered. Review verdict: CONDITIONAL\n142-\n143:<!-- /ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n144-## 13. KNOWN CONTEXT\n145-\n146-### Bounded Context Snapshot\n147-\n148-- **Target pointers:** `command-attach.ts` (`commandOnlyMentioned` at 422-453, call sites at 259, 504), `command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` (markup cases at 172-190), `doctor-install-presentation.txt` (accepted answers at 65-78), `doctor-install.yaml` (inputs at 46, ask step at 58), `doctor-install-contract.test.cjs` (runtime assertion at 238-244).\n149-- **Behavior claims:** `commandOnlyMentioned` returns true when every occurrence of a command name carries a refusal or question lead, so `attachCommand` withholds an offer on a refusal/question. The doctor presentation must name the runtimes `symlink-manifest.json` offers, and the contract test derives that list from the manifest.\n150-- **Reuse and conventions:** quote folding already normalizes `“”‘’` to straight quotes; tests use `it.each` tables; the doctor contract test reads assets by path and parses YAML with `yaml`.\n151-- **Review risks and gaps:** the manifest carries eight runtimes including `dsh`; the engine rejects unknown runtime names at `symlink-engine.cjs:435-438`; `command-attach.ts` has a gitignored compiled copy under `runtime/dist/` that already carries the new line.\n152-\n153----\n154-\n155-## 14. CROSS-REFERENCE STATUS\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"139:<!-- ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n140-## 11. NEXT FOCUS\n141-- **Dimension:** security. - **Focus area:** whether the mention guard can be evaded by quote placement to make the advisor offer or deliver a command the prompt refused, and whether the doctor install's printed writing commands can carry operator input beyond the values it validated. - **Reason:** the guard's purpose is to keep a mutating command from being offered on a refusal; iteration 1 found one reachable evasion, so the adversarial pass should map the family rather than add a second instance of it. - **Rotation status:** correctness and traceability reviewed; security next, maintainability last. - **Blocked/productive carry-forward:** traceability is productive (two P2s, both with a concrete mutation that keeps tests green); no approach is blocked. - **Required evidence:** compiled-module runs over quote/lead permutations (brace, quote, apostrophe, list joins), and the presentation's printed-command invariants at `doctor-install-presentation.txt:5` and `:139`. **Stop decision after iteration 1:** CONTINUE; `stopReason` none; `blockedBy` empty; the coverage gate names `security`, `traceability` and `maintainability` as the missing dimensions at that point, and `traceability` is now covered. Review verdict: CONDITIONAL\n142-\n143:<!-- /ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n144-## 13. KNOWN CONTEXT\n145-\n146-### Bounded Context Snapshot\n147-\n148-- **Target pointers:** `command-attach.ts` (`commandOnlyMentioned` at 422-453, call sites at 259, 504), `command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` (markup cases at 172-190), `doctor-install-presentation.txt` (accepted answers at 65-78), `doctor-install.yaml` (inputs at 46, ask step at 58), `doctor-install-contract.test.cjs` (runtime assertion at 238-244).\n149-- **Behavior claims:** `commandOnlyMentioned` returns true when every occurrence of a command name carries a refusal or question lead, so `attachCommand` withholds an offer on a refusal/question. The doctor presentation must name the runtimes `symlink-manifest.json` offers, and the contract test derives that list from the manifest.\n150-- **Reuse and conventions:** quote folding already normalizes `“”‘’` to straight quotes; tests use `it.each` tables; the doctor contract test reads assets by path and parses YAML with `yaml`.\n151-- **Review risks and gaps:** the manifest carries eight runtimes including `dsh`; the engine rejects unknown runtime names at `symlink-engine.cjs:435-438`; `command-attach.ts` has a gitignored compiled copy under `runtime/dist/` that already carries the new line.\n152-\n153----\n154-\n155-## 14. CROSS-REFERENCE STATUS\n"}],"providerCall"