{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794852805763,"sessionID":"ses_e1a82d918ffeSg4o2dc6d2Zt3H","part":{"partID":"prt_1e590080a002Hpt0hEEflr53rg","sessionID":"ses_e1a82d918ffeSg4o2dc6d2Zt3H","messageID":"msg_1e58fe684001BSjiEQCXzCsJOx","type":"tool","id":"call_650713a9ddab44dfba7e3926","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Review Iteration 004 — fixes-11\n\n**Lineage:** `fixes-11` (detached fan-out, review pass eleven)\n**Artifact dir:** `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/fixes-11`\n**Session:** `fanout-fixes-11-1794851543294-mlt3r6`\n\n## Dispatcher\n\n- **Operator review focus (bound):** review pass eleven, area `fixes`, per `review/review-brief-11.txt`. This iteration closed the rotation on the focus's own surfaces: the readability and drift cost of the quote fold's comment, the doctor install's accepted-answer sentence, and the contract test's duplicated count assertion.\n- **Dimension this iteration:** maintainability.\n- **Dimensions planned:** correctness (done), traceability (done), security (done), maintainability.\n- **Steer file:** absent at iteration start.\n\n## Files Reviewed\n\n| File | Under |\n|------|-------|\n| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts` | maintainability |\n| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` | maintainability |\n| `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-install-presentation.txt` | maintainability |\n| `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-install.yaml` | maintainability |\n| `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/doctor-install-contract.test.cjs` | maintainability |\n\n## Findings - New\n\n### P0 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n### P1 Findings\n\nNone new; `FIX11-P1-001` and `FIX11-P1-002` remain active.\n\n### P2 Findings\n\n1. **The fold comment claims quote marks around a name are dropped, but only the opening single quote is** -- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:413` -- The paragraph says \"quote marks around a name are dropped for the same reason\" and then adds the single-quote rule at `:415-417`, but the single-quote rule is one-sided: the closing quote survives. That same paragraph also breaks mid-sentence at `:417` (\"as \\\"don't\\\" or \\\"what's\\\". The\" / `:418` \"boundary before the lead…\"), so the paragraph that defines the guard's fold contract is the hardest part of the file to read.\nCase: a maintainer reading `:413` expects `do not run '/create:agent' or '/create:readme'` to behave like the double-quoted form; the closing quote is still present and the second command loses its refusal lead (iteration 1, `FIX11-P1-001`).\nFinding class: maintainability (comment overstates the fold and is split mid-sentence).\nScope proof: the comment block at `:409-421` and the fold at `:423-429` are the reviewed file's own changed lines; the behaviour is reproduced by the compiled module.\nAffected surface hints: `commandOnlyMentioned`'s fold, its comment, and every reader who extends the quote rule.\n\n2. **The accepted-answer sentence fuses the accepted list with \"the ones already there\"** -- `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-install-presentation.txt:78` -- The sentence reads \"A runtime name outside claude, codex, cursor, devin, dsh, opencode, pi and vibe or the ones already there, a shape outside the three, or an instruction word outside the two is not guessed.\" The coordination makes \"the ones already there\" part of what a name is \"outside\" of, which is the opposite of the rule: those names are accepted. The reader has to re-parse a sentence whose only job is to say which answers are accepted.\nCase: an operator answers `rust` and reads the sentence to learn whether it will be accepted; \"outside … or the ones already there\" can be read as \"outside the eight, or outside the detected ones\" rather than \"the eight and the detected ones are accepted\".\nFinding class: maintainability (user-facing wording that obscures the acceptance rule).\nScope proof: `:78` is the changed line in the reviewed diff; the accepted set is the eight manifest runtimes confirmed at `symlink-manifest.json` and `symlink-engine.cjs:435-438`.\nAffected surface hints: `/doctor:install` accepted answers, the guide's re-ask rule, and the contract test's exact-substring assertion at `doctor-install-contract.test.cjs:243`.\n\n3. **A contract assertion is now fully subsumed by the next line** -- `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/doctor-install-contract.test.cjs:239` -- `assert.doesNotMatch(PRESENTATION, /outside the seven/)` is implied by `:240`'s `assert.doesNotMatch(PRESENTATION, /outside the (?:seven|eight|nine)/)`: any text that fails the first line also fails the second. The line can never be the one that catches a regression, so it adds a maintenance stop without adding coverage.\nCase: change the presentation to \"outside the seven\" and run the test; line 239 fails, but line 240 fails with the same message on the same input, so 239 carries no independent signal.\nFinding class: maintainability (dead assertion duplicating the one below it).\nScope proof: both lines are in the reviewed test file; the first regex is a strict subset of the second alternation.\nAffected surface hints: the runtime-count guard in `doctor-install-contract.test.cjs`.\n\n## Traceability Checks\n\nNo new protocol was run this iteration. The maintainability pass cites the reviewed files' own comments, the manifest and engine evidence already established in iteration 2, and the compiled-module behaviour from iteration 1.\n\n## Integration Evidence\n\n- **Comment ↔ behaviour:** `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:413-417` ↔ `:423-429`. The comment is the only statement of the fold's contract; the closing-quote gap is what makes it worth correcting alongside the code fix.\n- **Sentence ↔ engine:** `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-install-presentation.txt:78` ↔ `symlink-engine.cjs:435-438`. The engine is the authority on which names are accepted; the sentence should read as \"these eight, or the detected ones\".\n- **Assertion ↔ assertion:** `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/doctor-install-contract.test.cjs:239` ↔ `:240`. The first is a strict subset of the second.\n- **Test title ↔ body:** already recorded as `FIX11-P2-001`; not repeated here.\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- **Two runtime-list surfaces.** The presentation names the runtimes in manifest order at `:58` and in sorted order at `:78`; the contract test checks only the sorted sentence (`test:243`). A maintainer reordering the manifest would see the test pass while the prompt list drifts. This is covered by `FIX11-P2-001`'s scope (the test does not check every surface it claims), so it is not raised as a fourth finding.\n- **Comment length.** The fold paragraph is one dense block covering five rules; a full rewrite is out of scope for a review, so the finding names the two concrete repairs (correct the symmetry claim, rejoin the split sentence) instead of asking for a restructure.\n- **Wording preference.** The accepted-answer sentence is understandable on a second read; the finding is scoped to the ambiguity a first-time operator hits, not to style preference.\n\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\n\n- The test table headings and `it.each` structure remain consistent with the surrounding file; the new cases do not break the table's naming convention.\n- `doctor-install.yaml:46` and `:58` remain internally consistent with each other and with the presentation's eight names.\n- No comment in the reviewed files carries an ephemeral artifact label, spec path, or requirement id; the durable WHY is preserved.\n- The new fold line at `command-attach.ts:427` is short, uses the file's existing chain style, and needs no helper extraction.\n\n## Ruled Out\n\n- **Naming inconsistency as a defect** — the presentation's two orders (manifest order in the prompt, sorted order in the accepted-answer sentence) are both complete and readable; only the test coverage differs, already recorded.\n- **Over-abstraction of the fold** — the one-line fold matches the surrounding chain of `.replace` calls; extracting a helper would add indirection for a single use.\n- **Test title drift as a maintainability finding** — already recorded once as `FIX11-P2-001` under traceability; repeating it here would double-count the same defect.\n\n## Next Focus\n\n- **Dimension:** cross-reference closure (all four dimensions covered; no new dimension remains).\n- **Focus area:** reconcile the active findings with the packet evidence, confirm no reviewed surface is unreviewed, and check whether the remaining work is a code fix, a test fix or an evidence fix for each active finding.\n- **Reason:** the rotation is complete; the next pass is a closure pass, not a new direction.\n- **Rotation status:** correctness, traceability, security and maintainability reviewed.\n- **Blocked/productive carry-forward:** maintainability is productive (three P2s, each with a concrete input); no approach is blocked.\n- **Required evidence:** the active finding list from the registry, the reviewed-file coverage table, and the stop decision.\n\n**Stop decision after iteration 3:** CONTINUE; `stopReason` none; `blockedBy` empty; the coverage gate named `maintainability` as the only missing dimension, and it is now covered.\n\nReview verdict: CONDITIONAL\n","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/fixes-11/iterations/iteration-004.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/fixes-11/iterations/iteration-004.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/fixes-11/iterations/iteration-004.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\":\"# Review Iteration 004 — fixes-11\\n\\n**Lineage:** `fixes-11` (detached fan-out, review pass eleven)\\n**Artifact dir:** `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/fixes-11`\\n**Session:** `fanout-fixes-11-1794851543294-mlt3r6`\\n\\n## Dispatcher\\n\\n- **Operator review focus (bound):** review pass eleven, area `fixes`, per `review/review-brief-11.txt`. This iteration closed the rotation on the focus's own surfaces: the readability and drift cost of the quote fold's comment, the doctor install's accepted-answer sentence, and the contract test's duplicated count assertion.\\n- **Dimension this iteration:** maintainability.\\n- **Dimensions planned:** correctness (done), traceability (done), security (done), maintainability.\\n- **Steer file:** absent at iteration start.\\n\\n## Files Reviewed\\n\\n| File | Under |\\n|------|-------|\\n| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts` | maintainability |\\n| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` | maintainability |\\n| `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-install-presentation.txt` | maintainability |\\n| `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-install.yaml` | maintainability |\\n| `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/doctor-install-contract.test.cjs` | maintainability |\\n\\n## Findings - New\\n\\n### P0 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### P1 Findings\\n\\nNone new; `FIX11-P1-001` and `FIX11-P1-002` remain active.\\n\\n### P2 Findings\\n\\n1. **The fold comment claims quote marks around a name are dropped, but only the opening single quote is** -- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:413` -- The paragraph says \\\"quote marks around a name are dropped for the same reason\\\" and then adds the single-quote rule at `:415-417`, but the single-quote rule is one-sided: the closing quote survives. That same paragraph also breaks mid-sentence at `:417` (\\\"as \\\\\\\"don't\\\\\\\" or \\\\\\\"what's\\\\\\\". The\\\" / `:418` \\\"boundary before the lead…\\\"), so the paragraph that defines the guard's fold contract is the hardest part of the file to read.\\nCase: a maintainer reading `:413` expects `do not run '/create:agent' or '/create:readme'` to behave like the double-quoted form; the closing quote is still present and the second command loses its refusal lead (iteration 1, `FIX11-P1-001`).\\nFinding class: maintainability (comment overstates the fold and is split mid-sentence).\\nScope proof: the comment block at `:409-421` and the fold at `:423-429` are the reviewed file's own changed lines; the behaviour is reproduced by the compiled module.\\nAffected surface hints: `commandOnlyMentioned`'s fold, its comment, and every reader who extends the quote rule.\\n\\n2. **The accepted-answer sentence fuses the accepted list with \\\"the ones already there\\\"** -- `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-install-presentation.txt:78` -- The sentence reads \\\"A runtime name outside claude, codex, cursor, devin, dsh, opencode, pi and vibe or the ones already there, a shape outside the three, or an instruction word outside the two is not guessed.\\\" The coordination makes \\\"the ones already there\\\" part of what a name is \\\"outside\\\" of, which is the opposite of the rule: those names are accepted. The reader has to re-parse a sentence whose only job is to say which answers are accepted.\\nCase: an operator answers `rust` and reads the sentence to learn whether it will be accepted; \\\"outside … or the ones already there\\\" can be read as \\\"outside the eight, or outside the detected ones\\\" rather than \\\"the eight and the detected ones are accepted\\\".\\nFinding class: maintainability (user-facing wording that obscures the acceptance rule).\\nScope proof: `:78` is the changed line in the reviewed diff; the accepted set is the eight manifest runtimes confirmed at `symlink-manifest.json` and `symlink-engine.cjs:435-438`.\\nAffected surface hints: `/doctor:install` accepted answers, the guide's re-ask rule, and the contract test's exact-substring assertion at `doctor-install-contract.test.cjs:243`.\\n\\n3. **A contract assertion is now fully subsumed by the next line** -- `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/doctor-install-contract.test.cjs:239` -- `assert.doesNotMatch(PRESENTATION, /outside the seven/)` is implied by `:240`'s `assert.doesNotMatch(PRESENTATION, /outside the (?:seven|eight|nine)/)`: any text that fails the first line also fails the second. The line can never be the one that catches a regression, so it adds a maintenance stop without adding coverage.\\nCase: change the presentation to \\\"outside the seven\\\" and run the test; line 239 fails, but line 240 fails with the same message on the same input, so 239 carries no independent signal.\\nFinding class: maintainability (dead assertion duplicating the one below it).\\nScope proof: both lines are in the reviewed test file; the first regex is a strict subset of the second alternation.\\nAffected surface hints: the runtime-count guard in `doctor-install-contract.test.cjs`.\\n\\n## Traceability Checks\\n\\nNo new protocol was run this iteration. The maintainability pass cites the reviewed files' own comments, the manifest and engine evidence already established in iteration 2, and the compiled-module behaviour from iteration 1.\\n\\n## Integration Evidence\\n\\n- **Comment ↔ behaviour:** `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:413-417` ↔ `:423-429`. The comment is the only statement of the fold's contract; the closing-quote gap is what makes it worth correcting alongside the code fix.\\n- **Sentence ↔ engine:** `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-install-presentation.txt:78` ↔ `symlink-engine.cjs:435-438`. The engine is the authority on which names are accepted; the sentence should read as \\\"these eight, or the detected ones\\\".\\n- **Assertion ↔ assertion:** `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/doctor-install-contract.test.cjs:239` ↔ `:240`. The first is a strict subset of the second.\\n- **Test title ↔ body:** already recorded as `FIX11-P2-001`; not repeated here.\\n\\n## Edge Cases\\n\\n- **Two runtime-list surfaces.** The presentation names the runtimes in manifest order at `:58` and in sorted order at `:78`; the contract test checks only the sorted sentence (`test:243`). A maintainer reordering the manifest would see the test pass while the prompt list drifts. This is covered by `FIX11-P2-001`'s scope (the test does not check every surface it claims), so it is not raised as a fourth finding.\\n- **Comment length.** The fold paragraph is one dense block covering five rules; a full rewrite is out of scope for a review, so the finding names the two concrete repairs (correct the symmetry claim, rejoin the split sentence) instead of asking for a restructure.\\n- **Wording preference.** The accepted-answer sentence is understandable on a second read; the finding is scoped to the ambiguity a first-time operator hits, not to style preference.\\n\\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\\n\\n- The test table headings and `it.each` structure remain consistent with the surrounding file; the new cases do not break the table's naming convention.\\n- `doctor-install.yaml:46` and `:58` remain internally consistent with each other and with the presentation's eight names.\\n- No comment in the reviewed files carries an ephemeral artifact label, spec path, or requirement id; the durable WHY is preserved.\\n- The new fold line at `command-attach.ts:427` is short, uses the file's existing chain style, and needs no helper extraction.\\n\\n## Ruled Out\\n\\n- **Naming inconsistency as a defect** — the presentation's two orders (manifest order in the prompt, sorted order in the accepted-answer sentence) are both complete and readable; only the test coverage differs, already recorded.\\n- **Over-abstraction of the fold** — the one-line fold matches the surrounding chain of `.replace` calls; extracting a helper would add indirection for a single use.\\n- **Test title drift as a maintainability finding** — already recorded once as `FIX11-P2-001` under traceability; repeating it here would double-count the same defect.\\n\\n## Next Focus\\n\\n- **Dimension:** cross-reference closure (all four dimensions covered; no new dimension remains).\\n- **Focus area:** reconcile the active findings with the packet evidence, confirm no reviewed surface is unreviewed, and check whether the remaining work is a code fix, a test fix or an evidence fix for each active finding.\\n- **Reason:** the rotation is complete; the next pass is a closure pass, not a new direction.\\n- **Rotation status:** correctness, traceability, security and maintainability reviewed.\\n- **Blocked/productive carry-forward:** maintainability is productive (three P2s, each with a concrete input); no approach is blocked.\\n- **Required evidence:** the active finding list from the registry, the reviewed-file coverage table, and the stop decision.\\n\\n**Stop decision after iteration 3:** CONTINUE; `stopReason` none; `blockedBy` empty; the coverage gate named `maintainability` as the only missing dimension, and it is now covered.\\n\\nReview verdict: CONDITIONAL\\n\",\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/fixes-11/iterations/iteration-004.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794852784138,"end":1794852805763}}}}
