{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794852922155,"sessionID":"ses_e1a82d918ffeSg4o2dc6d2Zt3H","part":{"partID":"prt_1e591e3f9002Tpx7lP2JToHA0E","sessionID":"ses_e1a82d918ffeSg4o2dc6d2Zt3H","messageID":"msg_1e591d397001dVjOeN2sFTOTm1","type":"tool","id":"call_c6260ec66ffd4cd4bcd88411","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Review Iteration 005 — fixes-11\n\n**Lineage:** `fixes-11` (detached fan-out, review pass eleven)\n**Artifact dir:** `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/fixes-11`\n**Session:** `fanout-fixes-11-1794851543294-mlt3r6`\n\n## Dispatcher\n\n- **Operator review focus (bound):** review pass eleven, area `fixes`, per `review/review-brief-11.txt`. This iteration is the closure pass for the focus: it re-checked every active finding against the current bytes of the reviewed files, confirmed the five scope paths each carry more than one dimension, and reconciled the packet evidence (REQ-006, AC-006, T010/T011) with what the code and tests actually do.\n- **Dimension this iteration:** traceability (cross-reference closure).\n- **Dimensions planned:** all four reviewed; this pass re-checks coverage.\n- **Steer file:** absent at iteration start.\n\n## Files Reviewed\n\n| File | Under |\n|------|-------|\n| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts` | traceability |\n| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` | traceability |\n| `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-install-presentation.txt` | traceability |\n| `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-install.yaml` | traceability |\n| `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/doctor-install-contract.test.cjs` | traceability |\n\n## Findings - New\n\n### P0 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n### P1 Findings\n\nNone new; `FIX11-P1-001` and `FIX11-P1-002` remain active.\n\n### P2 Findings\n\nNone new.\n\n## Traceability Checks\n\n| Protocol | Status | Evidence |\n|----------|--------|----------|\n| `spec_code` | partial | Re-read `spec.md:134` (REQ-006) against `command-attach.ts:427` and `:259`: the quoted single-command shape is implemented; the quoted or-list shape (`FIX11-P1-001`) and the retired-name guard (`FIX11-P1-002`) are not. The doctor half still holds at `presentation:78`, `yaml:58` and the manifest. |\n| `checklist_evidence` | partial | Re-read `acceptance-criteria.md:59` (AC-006, `Met`) and `tasks.md:60-61` (T010/T011): the stated evidence is present and reproducible; the AC's given remains narrower than REQ-006, and the contract test's runtime assertion still reads the presentation only. |\n\n## Active Finding Recheck\n\n| Finding | Severity | Recheck at current bytes | Still active |\n|---------|----------|--------------------------|--------------|\n| `FIX11-P1-001` | P1 | `command-attach.ts:427` still strips only the opening quote; `command-attach.ts:385` and `:438-442` still cannot bridge the closing quote; the compiled module still returns `false` for `do not run '/create:agent' or '/create:readme'` and `attachCommand` still returns `/create:readme`. | Yes |\n| `FIX11-P1-002` | P1 | `command-attach.ts:243` still maps `/create:skill` → `/create:sk-skill` before the guard at `:259`; `typedCommandForTop` still returns the successor for a refusal of the old name, and `attachCommand` still returns it for a single-target route. | Yes |\n| `FIX11-P2-001` | P2 | `doctor-install-contract.test.cjs:238-244` still asserts only `PRESENTATION` against the manifest; no assertion reads `WORKFLOW` for a runtime name. | Yes |\n| `FIX11-P2-002` | P2 | `acceptance-criteria.md:59` still names only the single-command prompt. | Yes |\n| `FIX11-P2-003` | P2 | `command-attach.ts:413` still claims quote marks around a name are dropped; `:417-418` still splits mid-sentence. | Yes |\n| `FIX11-P2-004` | P2 | `presentation:78` still fuses the accepted list with \"the ones already there\". | Yes |\n| `FIX11-P2-005` | P2 | `doctor-install-contract.test.cjs:239` is still a strict subset of `:240`. | Yes |\n\nNo finding was resolved or downgraded this iteration; no code changed under review (`git status` shows only the lineage directory and the shared observability log modified).\n\n## Integration Evidence\n\n- **Coverage:** all five scope files carry correctness, traceability, security and maintainability reads (iterations 1-4), so no scope file is single-dimension.\n- **Packet → code:** REQ-006's two halves map to `command-attach.ts:427` (quote fold) and the four doctor surfaces (`presentation:78`, `yaml:58`, `symlink-manifest.json`, `symlink-engine.cjs:435-438`).\n- **Code → test:** the quote fold's tests cover four single-command mention shapes and two request shapes (`command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:172-190`); no test covers the or-list shape or the retired alias. The doctor contract test covers the presentation sentence (`test:243`) but not the workflow list.\n- **Holdout hygiene:** no prompt corpus file was opened; the holdout gate was read by count only, per the brief's rule.\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- **Registry vs narrative.** The registry lists all seven active findings and computes two P1 and five P2; the narrative counts match the delta rows. No discrepancy was found.\n- **Closure depends on fixes, not further review.** Every active finding has a named file:line and a concrete input; none is blocked on missing evidence, so the next step is remediation, not another dimension.\n- **Doctor membership is clean.** The only remaining doctor findings are the test-coverage and wording ones; the runtime set itself agrees across every surface.\n\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\n\n- The five scope files are all present at the reviewed commit and unchanged during the review.\n- The review packet's active findings all have file:line evidence; no finding relies only on inference.\n- No stale compiled advisor build: `runtime/dist/runtime/lib/command-attach.js` carries the same fold and the same mapping order as the source.\n- No holdout text was read or printed; no prompt corpus file was opened.\n\n## Ruled Out\n\n- **A missing dimension or scope file** — all four dimensions and all five scope paths are covered; the only gap is remediation of the active findings.\n- **A registry/narrative mismatch** — counts and ids agree across registry, iterations and deltas.\n- **A stale review artifact** — every active finding was re-read at the current bytes and still holds.\n\n## Next Focus\n\n- **Dimension:** closure verification (no new dimension).\n- **Focus area:** confirm the stop decision against the registry and prepare the lineage for synthesis; do not open a new review direction.\n- **Reason:** every dimension is covered and every active finding is verified; further review would repeat evidence rather than add signal.\n- **Rotation status:** complete for all four dimensions.\n- **Blocked/productive carry-forward:** none blocked; the productive approaches are recorded in the strategy.\n- **Required evidence:** the stop decision from `convergence.cjs` and the registry counts.\n\n**Stop decision after iteration 4:** CONTINUE; `stopReason` none; `blockedBy` empty; no dimension is missing, but the rolling signal was still above the convergence threshold.\n\nReview verdict: CONDITIONAL\n","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/fixes-11/iterations/iteration-005.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/fixes-11/iterations/iteration-005.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/fixes-11/iterations/iteration-005.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\":\"# Review Iteration 005 — fixes-11\\n\\n**Lineage:** `fixes-11` (detached fan-out, review pass eleven)\\n**Artifact dir:** `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/fixes-11`\\n**Session:** `fanout-fixes-11-1794851543294-mlt3r6`\\n\\n## Dispatcher\\n\\n- **Operator review focus (bound):** review pass eleven, area `fixes`, per `review/review-brief-11.txt`. This iteration is the closure pass for the focus: it re-checked every active finding against the current bytes of the reviewed files, confirmed the five scope paths each carry more than one dimension, and reconciled the packet evidence (REQ-006, AC-006, T010/T011) with what the code and tests actually do.\\n- **Dimension this iteration:** traceability (cross-reference closure).\\n- **Dimensions planned:** all four reviewed; this pass re-checks coverage.\\n- **Steer file:** absent at iteration start.\\n\\n## Files Reviewed\\n\\n| File | Under |\\n|------|-------|\\n| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts` | traceability |\\n| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` | traceability |\\n| `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-install-presentation.txt` | traceability |\\n| `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-install.yaml` | traceability |\\n| `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/doctor-install-contract.test.cjs` | traceability |\\n\\n## Findings - New\\n\\n### P0 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### P1 Findings\\n\\nNone new; `FIX11-P1-001` and `FIX11-P1-002` remain active.\\n\\n### P2 Findings\\n\\nNone new.\\n\\n## Traceability Checks\\n\\n| Protocol | Status | Evidence |\\n|----------|--------|----------|\\n| `spec_code` | partial | Re-read `spec.md:134` (REQ-006) against `command-attach.ts:427` and `:259`: the quoted single-command shape is implemented; the quoted or-list shape (`FIX11-P1-001`) and the retired-name guard (`FIX11-P1-002`) are not. The doctor half still holds at `presentation:78`, `yaml:58` and the manifest. |\\n| `checklist_evidence` | partial | Re-read `acceptance-criteria.md:59` (AC-006, `Met`) and `tasks.md:60-61` (T010/T011): the stated evidence is present and reproducible; the AC's given remains narrower than REQ-006, and the contract test's runtime assertion still reads the presentation only. |\\n\\n## Active Finding Recheck\\n\\n| Finding | Severity | Recheck at current bytes | Still active |\\n|---------|----------|--------------------------|--------------|\\n| `FIX11-P1-001` | P1 | `command-attach.ts:427` still strips only the opening quote; `command-attach.ts:385` and `:438-442` still cannot bridge the closing quote; the compiled module still returns `false` for `do not run '/create:agent' or '/create:readme'` and `attachCommand` still returns `/create:readme`. | Yes |\\n| `FIX11-P1-002` | P1 | `command-attach.ts:243` still maps `/create:skill` → `/create:sk-skill` before the guard at `:259`; `typedCommandForTop` still returns the successor for a refusal of the old name, and `attachCommand` still returns it for a single-target route. | Yes |\\n| `FIX11-P2-001` | P2 | `doctor-install-contract.test.cjs:238-244` still asserts only `PRESENTATION` against the manifest; no assertion reads `WORKFLOW` for a runtime name. | Yes |\\n| `FIX11-P2-002` | P2 | `acceptance-criteria.md:59` still names only the single-command prompt. | Yes |\\n| `FIX11-P2-003` | P2 | `command-attach.ts:413` still claims quote marks around a name are dropped; `:417-418` still splits mid-sentence. | Yes |\\n| `FIX11-P2-004` | P2 | `presentation:78` still fuses the accepted list with \\\"the ones already there\\\". | Yes |\\n| `FIX11-P2-005` | P2 | `doctor-install-contract.test.cjs:239` is still a strict subset of `:240`. | Yes |\\n\\nNo finding was resolved or downgraded this iteration; no code changed under review (`git status` shows only the lineage directory and the shared observability log modified).\\n\\n## Integration Evidence\\n\\n- **Coverage:** all five scope files carry correctness, traceability, security and maintainability reads (iterations 1-4), so no scope file is single-dimension.\\n- **Packet → code:** REQ-006's two halves map to `command-attach.ts:427` (quote fold) and the four doctor surfaces (`presentation:78`, `yaml:58`, `symlink-manifest.json`, `symlink-engine.cjs:435-438`).\\n- **Code → test:** the quote fold's tests cover four single-command mention shapes and two request shapes (`command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:172-190`); no test covers the or-list shape or the retired alias. The doctor contract test covers the presentation sentence (`test:243`) but not the workflow list.\\n- **Holdout hygiene:** no prompt corpus file was opened; the holdout gate was read by count only, per the brief's rule.\\n\\n## Edge Cases\\n\\n- **Registry vs narrative.** The registry lists all seven active findings and computes two P1 and five P2; the narrative counts match the delta rows. No discrepancy was found.\\n- **Closure depends on fixes, not further review.** Every active finding has a named file:line and a concrete input; none is blocked on missing evidence, so the next step is remediation, not another dimension.\\n- **Doctor membership is clean.** The only remaining doctor findings are the test-coverage and wording ones; the runtime set itself agrees across every surface.\\n\\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\\n\\n- The five scope files are all present at the reviewed commit and unchanged during the review.\\n- The review packet's active findings all have file:line evidence; no finding relies only on inference.\\n- No stale compiled advisor build: `runtime/dist/runtime/lib/command-attach.js` carries the same fold and the same mapping order as the source.\\n- No holdout text was read or printed; no prompt corpus file was opened.\\n\\n## Ruled Out\\n\\n- **A missing dimension or scope file** — all four dimensions and all five scope paths are covered; the only gap is remediation of the active findings.\\n- **A registry/narrative mismatch** — counts and ids agree across registry, iterations and deltas.\\n- **A stale review artifact** — every active finding was re-read at the current bytes and still holds.\\n\\n## Next Focus\\n\\n- **Dimension:** closure verification (no new dimension).\\n- **Focus area:** confirm the stop decision against the registry and prepare the lineage for synthesis; do not open a new review direction.\\n- **Reason:** every dimension is covered and every active finding is verified; further review would repeat evidence rather than add signal.\\n- **Rotation status:** complete for all four dimensions.\\n- **Blocked/productive carry-forward:** none blocked; the productive approaches are recorded in the strategy.\\n- **Required evidence:** the stop decision from `convergence.cjs` and the registry counts.\\n\\n**Stop decision after iteration 4:** CONTINUE; `stopReason` none; `blockedBy` empty; no dimension is missing, but the rolling signal was still above the convergence threshold.\\n\\nReview verdict: CONDITIONAL\\n\",\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/fixes-11/iterations/iteration-005.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794852905977,"end":1794852922155}}}}
