{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794852994129,"sessionID":"ses_e1a82d918ffeSg4o2dc6d2Zt3H","part":{"partID":"prt_1e5930c790014Xc2nnKjh61g3y","sessionID":"ses_e1a82d918ffeSg4o2dc6d2Zt3H","messageID":"msg_1e592f8d80010Ec7k6bf1MJHrR","type":"tool","id":"call_1fb73702c29a411c99c5d4cf","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Review Iteration 006 — fixes-11\n\n**Lineage:** `fixes-11` (detached fan-out, review pass eleven)\n**Artifact dir:** `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/fixes-11`\n**Session:** `fanout-fixes-11-1794851543294-mlt3r6`\n\n## Dispatcher\n\n- **Operator review focus (bound):** review pass eleven, area `fixes`, per `review/review-brief-11.txt`. This iteration is a verification replay of the focus: it re-ran the two reachable evasions, re-read the seven active findings, and confirmed the reviewed bytes have not changed since iteration 5.\n- **Dimension this iteration:** correctness (verification replay).\n- **Dimensions planned:** all four covered; this pass re-checks the two P1 findings.\n- **Steer file:** absent at iteration start.\n\n## Files Reviewed\n\n| File | Under |\n|------|-------|\n| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts` | correctness |\n| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` | correctness |\n| `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-install-presentation.txt` | correctness |\n| `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-install.yaml` | correctness |\n| `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/doctor-install-contract.test.cjs` | correctness |\n\n## Findings - New\n\n### P0 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n### P1 Findings\n\nNone new; `FIX11-P1-001` and `FIX11-P1-002` remain active and reproduce.\n\n### P2 Findings\n\nNone new.\n\n## Traceability Checks\n\nNo new protocol was run; this pass is a replay of the evidence already recorded, and the audit trail is the same registry and delta rows from iterations 1-5.\n\n## Verification Replay\n\n| Probe | Result | Reading |\n|-------|--------|---------|\n| `commandOnlyMentioned(\"do not run '/create:agent' or '/create:readme', just explain them\", \"/create:readme\")` | `false` | The quoted or-list refusal is still not read (`FIX11-P1-001`). |\n| `attachCommand(\"sk-doc\", {single target sk-create-readme}, same prompt)` | `/create:readme` | The refused command is still offered. |\n| `typedCommandForTop(\"sk-doc\", \"do not run /create:skill yet, just explain\")` | `{\"command\":\"/create:sk-skill\",\"policy\":\"start\",\"ownerSkillId\":\"sk-doc\"}` | The retired-name refusal is still bypassed (`FIX11-P1-002`). |\n| `attachCommand(\"sk-doc\", {single target sk-create-skill}, same prompt)` | `/create:sk-skill` | The successor is still offered on the refusal. |\n| `commandOnlyMentioned(\"do not run /create:readme yet\", \"/create:readme\")` | `true` | Control: the canonical quoted refusal is read. |\n| `commandOnlyMentioned(\"do not run /create:sk-skill yet\", \"/create:sk-skill\")` | `true` | Control: the canonical successor name is read. |\n\nThe controls isolate both failures to the mapped or quoted name rather than to the guard's lead grammar.\n\n## Integration Evidence\n\n- Both probes ran against `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/dist/runtime/lib/command-attach.js`, the build the shipped advisor loads, not a hand copy.\n- `git status --short` shows no reviewed file modified during the review (`command-attach.ts`, the guards test, the doctor presentation, the doctor workflow and the contract test are all clean); the only tracked modification is the shared observability log.\n- The registry still holds two P1 and five P2 findings with no transitions; no finding was resolved, merged or downgraded since iteration 4.\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- **Convergence signal vs active P1s.** The convergence script's rolling signal is a novelty measure, not a resolution measure: it can stop the loop while P1 findings remain active. The verdict stays CONDITIONAL for that reason, and the synthesis report records the open findings rather than a pass.\n- **Replay vs new review.** This pass adds no new direction; a further iteration would repeat the same probes, so the loop terminates on the stop decision rather than on exhaustion of ideas.\n\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\n\n- The two administration controls above hold: canonical quoted refusals and canonical retired-name refusals are read correctly.\n- No reviewed file was modified; the review remained observation-only.\n- No holdout prompt text was read or printed; no prompt corpus file was opened in this pass.\n- All four dimensions and all five scope paths remain covered; the registry and narrative counts agree.\n\n## Ruled Out\n\n- **A regression introduced between iterations 5 and 6** — the reviewed bytes are unchanged and both probes reproduce identically.\n- **A guard failure on the canonical names** — both canonical controls return `true`; the failures are specific to the quoted or-list and the retired alias.\n- **A missing finding in the registry** — seven active findings, matching iterations 1-4 and the deltas.\n\n## Next Focus\n\n- **Dimension:** none; the loop is at its stop decision.\n- **Focus area:** synthesis and remediation planning for the two P1 and five P2 findings.\n- **Reason:** the stop decision is the loop's terminal signal; a further iteration would repeat the replay.\n- **Rotation status:** complete.\n- **Blocked/productive carry-forward:** no approach is blocked; the productive approaches are recorded in the strategy.\n- **Required evidence:** the stop decision from `convergence.cjs` and the registry counts.\n\n**Stop decision after iteration 5:** CONTINUE; `stopReason` none; `blockedBy` empty; the rolling signal sat at 0.100 with the noise floor already stopped, so one zero-novelty pass was still required.\n\nReview verdict: CONDITIONAL\n","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/fixes-11/iterations/iteration-006.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/fixes-11/iterations/iteration-006.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/fixes-11/iterations/iteration-006.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\":\"# Review Iteration 006 — fixes-11\\n\\n**Lineage:** `fixes-11` (detached fan-out, review pass eleven)\\n**Artifact dir:** `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/fixes-11`\\n**Session:** `fanout-fixes-11-1794851543294-mlt3r6`\\n\\n## Dispatcher\\n\\n- **Operator review focus (bound):** review pass eleven, area `fixes`, per `review/review-brief-11.txt`. This iteration is a verification replay of the focus: it re-ran the two reachable evasions, re-read the seven active findings, and confirmed the reviewed bytes have not changed since iteration 5.\\n- **Dimension this iteration:** correctness (verification replay).\\n- **Dimensions planned:** all four covered; this pass re-checks the two P1 findings.\\n- **Steer file:** absent at iteration start.\\n\\n## Files Reviewed\\n\\n| File | Under |\\n|------|-------|\\n| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts` | correctness |\\n| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` | correctness |\\n| `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-install-presentation.txt` | correctness |\\n| `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-install.yaml` | correctness |\\n| `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/doctor-install-contract.test.cjs` | correctness |\\n\\n## Findings - New\\n\\n### P0 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### P1 Findings\\n\\nNone new; `FIX11-P1-001` and `FIX11-P1-002` remain active and reproduce.\\n\\n### P2 Findings\\n\\nNone new.\\n\\n## Traceability Checks\\n\\nNo new protocol was run; this pass is a replay of the evidence already recorded, and the audit trail is the same registry and delta rows from iterations 1-5.\\n\\n## Verification Replay\\n\\n| Probe | Result | Reading |\\n|-------|--------|---------|\\n| `commandOnlyMentioned(\\\"do not run '/create:agent' or '/create:readme', just explain them\\\", \\\"/create:readme\\\")` | `false` | The quoted or-list refusal is still not read (`FIX11-P1-001`). |\\n| `attachCommand(\\\"sk-doc\\\", {single target sk-create-readme}, same prompt)` | `/create:readme` | The refused command is still offered. |\\n| `typedCommandForTop(\\\"sk-doc\\\", \\\"do not run /create:skill yet, just explain\\\")` | `{\\\"command\\\":\\\"/create:sk-skill\\\",\\\"policy\\\":\\\"start\\\",\\\"ownerSkillId\\\":\\\"sk-doc\\\"}` | The retired-name refusal is still bypassed (`FIX11-P1-002`). |\\n| `attachCommand(\\\"sk-doc\\\", {single target sk-create-skill}, same prompt)` | `/create:sk-skill` | The successor is still offered on the refusal. |\\n| `commandOnlyMentioned(\\\"do not run /create:readme yet\\\", \\\"/create:readme\\\")` | `true` | Control: the canonical quoted refusal is read. |\\n| `commandOnlyMentioned(\\\"do not run /create:sk-skill yet\\\", \\\"/create:sk-skill\\\")` | `true` | Control: the canonical successor name is read. |\\n\\nThe controls isolate both failures to the mapped or quoted name rather than to the guard's lead grammar.\\n\\n## Integration Evidence\\n\\n- Both probes ran against `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/dist/runtime/lib/command-attach.js`, the build the shipped advisor loads, not a hand copy.\\n- `git status --short` shows no reviewed file modified during the review (`command-attach.ts`, the guards test, the doctor presentation, the doctor workflow and the contract test are all clean); the only tracked modification is the shared observability log.\\n- The registry still holds two P1 and five P2 findings with no transitions; no finding was resolved, merged or downgraded since iteration 4.\\n\\n## Edge Cases\\n\\n- **Convergence signal vs active P1s.** The convergence script's rolling signal is a novelty measure, not a resolution measure: it can stop the loop while P1 findings remain active. The verdict stays CONDITIONAL for that reason, and the synthesis report records the open findings rather than a pass.\\n- **Replay vs new review.** This pass adds no new direction; a further iteration would repeat the same probes, so the loop terminates on the stop decision rather than on exhaustion of ideas.\\n\\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\\n\\n- The two administration controls above hold: canonical quoted refusals and canonical retired-name refusals are read correctly.\\n- No reviewed file was modified; the review remained observation-only.\\n- No holdout prompt text was read or printed; no prompt corpus file was opened in this pass.\\n- All four dimensions and all five scope paths remain covered; the registry and narrative counts agree.\\n\\n## Ruled Out\\n\\n- **A regression introduced between iterations 5 and 6** — the reviewed bytes are unchanged and both probes reproduce identically.\\n- **A guard failure on the canonical names** — both canonical controls return `true`; the failures are specific to the quoted or-list and the retired alias.\\n- **A missing finding in the registry** — seven active findings, matching iterations 1-4 and the deltas.\\n\\n## Next Focus\\n\\n- **Dimension:** none; the loop is at its stop decision.\\n- **Focus area:** synthesis and remediation planning for the two P1 and five P2 findings.\\n- **Reason:** the stop decision is the loop's terminal signal; a further iteration would repeat the replay.\\n- **Rotation status:** complete.\\n- **Blocked/productive carry-forward:** no approach is blocked; the productive approaches are recorded in the strategy.\\n- **Required evidence:** the stop decision from `convergence.cjs` and the registry counts.\\n\\n**Stop decision after iteration 5:** CONTINUE; `stopReason` none; `blockedBy` empty; the rolling signal sat at 0.100 with the noise floor already stopped, so one zero-novelty pass was still required.\\n\\nReview verdict: CONDITIONAL\\n\",\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/fixes-11/iterations/iteration-006.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794852981881,"end":1794852994129}}}}
