{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794853182086,"sessionID":"ses_e1a82d918ffeSg4o2dc6d2Zt3H","part":{"id":"prt_1e5961a86001aaTSS3vTQvthCq","sessionID":"ses_e1a82d918ffeSg4o2dc6d2Zt3H","messageID":"msg_1e59611c6001C0lyEjKJNGFQwH","type":"step-start","snapshot":"3efae4e0a6fc4627578b16b62e501b5ea3299a3b"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794853182556,"sessionID":"ses_e1a82d918ffeSg4o2dc6d2Zt3H","part":{"partID":"prt_1e5961a87002pzCPbU6BwFSQB9","sessionID":"ses_e1a82d918ffeSg4o2dc6d2Zt3H","messageID":"msg_1e59611c6001C0lyEjKJNGFQwH","type":"tool","id":"call_40a6d71a2e7b40e0b76dfdb2","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"limit":180,"offset":1996,"path":".skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review.yaml"},"output":"Read file .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review.yaml, lines 1996-2175\n1996:             active_p0: \"active_p0\"\n1997:             active_p1: \"active_p1\"\n1998:             active_p2: \"active_p2\"\n1999:             search_debt_count: \"search_debt\"\n2000:           on_fail: \"Halt with STATUS=FAIL through step_release_lock. The values the merge bound are the authority on a fan-out root, so an unreadable bound value must stop the run rather than let a verdict be guessed.\"\n2001:         if_absent:\n2002:           command: |\n2003:             node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/review-verdict.cjs \\\n2004:               --registry-path \"{state_paths.findings_registry}\" \\\n2005:               --state-log \"{state_paths.state_log}\"\n2006:           working_directory: \"{repo_root}\"\n2007:           wait_for_completion: true\n2008:           bind_from_output:\n2009:             verdict: \"verdict\"\n2010:             has_advisories: \"has_advisories\"\n2011:             active_p0: \"active_p0\"\n2012:             active_p1: \"active_p1\"\n2013:             active_p2: \"active_p2\"\n2014:             search_debt_count: \"search_debt\"\n2015:           on_fail: \"Halt with STATUS=FAIL through step_release_lock. A non-zero exit means the registry or the state log could not be read, so this stop has no verdict yet and none may be assumed.\"\n2016:         outputs:\n2017:           - verdict: \"PASS | CONDITIONAL | FAIL\"\n2018:           - has_advisories: \"Boolean true when verdict is PASS and any active P2 findings exist\"\n2019:           - active_p0: \"Active P0 count the verdict used\"\n2020:           - active_p1: \"Active P1 count the verdict used\"\n2021:           - active_p2: \"Active P2 count the verdict used\"\n2022:           - ac_coverage_signal: \"exempt | disabled | pass | advisory-shortfall\"\n2023:         contract: |\n2024:           Every iteration-NNN.md must end with exactly: \"Review verdict: PASS\" (or CONDITIONAL or FAIL).\n2025:           Downstream automation parses this final line via exact string match — do not vary the format.\n2026: \n2027:       step_emit_resource_map:\n2028:         skip_when: \"config.fanout is present\"\n2029:         action: \"Emit {state_paths.resource_map_output} from converged review deltas unless config.resource_map.emit is false\"\n2030:         dry_run_boundary: \"reducer-refresh\"\n2031:         command: \"node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/reduce-state.cjs {spec_folder} {reducer_artifact_arg} --create-missing-anchors --emit-resource-map\"\n2032:         read:\n2033:           - \"{state_paths.config}\"\n2034:           - \"{state_paths.delta_dir}/iter-*.jsonl\"\n2035:         write:\n2036:           - \"{state_paths.resource_map_output}\"\n2037:         guarantee: \"Reducer skips cleanly when config.resource_map.emit == false and writes a deterministic resource-map when enabled.\"\n2038:         note: \"A fan-out root has no root state log before closeout, so the root reducer would fail on the missing file. Each lineage emits its own map, so the report names the ones that exist at {artifact_dir}/lineages/*/resource-map.md.\"\n2039: \n2040:       step_resource_map_coverage_gate:\n2041:         action: \"If resource_map_present, compute the Resource Map Coverage Gate synthesis inputs; otherwise preserve the skip note\"\n2042:         note: \"Cross-check target_files from {spec_folder}/applied/T-*.md against {spec_folder}/resource-map.md. Report touched entries, untouched entries split into expected-by-scope vs gap, and implementation paths absent from the map. Findings raised here use category resource-map-coverage with severity calibrated to the gate outcome.\"\n2043: \n2044:       step_compile_review_report:\n2045:         action: \"Compile review/review-report.md with 9 core sections, a conditional Resource Map Coverage Gate section, and an embedded Planning Packet\"\n2046:         dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n2047:         instructions: |\n2048:           **Zero-iteration stop:** When {state_paths.state_log} holds no line with type \"iteration\" (on a fan-out root, when none of the lineage state logs under {state_paths.packet_dir}/lineages/ holds one), the review did not run, and the report says so instead of reporting on work that never happened:\n2049:              - Executive Summary: open with `Review did not run`, state the stop reason and `0 iterations dispatched`, keep the verdict and hasAdvisories bound by step_derive_verdict unchanged, and state that the P0/P1/P2 counts mean not examined rather than clean.\n2050:              - Planning Trigger: state that `/speckit:plan` is not required, and set the Planning Packet to `triggered: false` and `reviewDidNotRun: true` with `remediationWorkstreams: []`, keeping every other required key from section 2 at an empty value.\n2051:              - Next step: name `/deep:review` again with a duration budget or iteration cap that allows at least one pass.\n2052:              - Sections 3 to 8: give each a single line saying the review did not run.\n2053: \n2054:           Create review/review-report.md with the following sections:\n2055: \n2056:           1. **Executive Summary**\n2057:              - Overall verdict: PASS | CONDITIONAL | FAIL\n2058:              - hasAdvisories: true when PASS carries active P2 items\n2059:              - P0/P1/P2 counts: {active_p0}, {active_p1}, {active_p2}, the counts the verdict used, stated as such\n2060:              - Self-check outcomes: each finding the adversarial self-check confirmed, downgraded or called a false positive. On a single-executor run the counts above already reflect them, so list them for reference\n2061:              - Review scope summary\n2062:              - Operator review focus: config.reviewFocus verbatim, or omit this line when it is null\n2063: \n2064:           2. **Planning Trigger**\n2065:              - State whether `/speckit:plan` is required\n2066:              - Include a fenced `json` block labeled `Planning Packet`\n2067:              - The packet MUST include: `triggered`, `verdict`, `hasAdvisories`, `activeFindings`, `remediationWorkstreams`, `specSeed`, `planSeed`, `findingClasses`, `affectedSurfacesSeed`, `fixCompletenessRequired`\n2068:              - Build `activeFindings`, `findingClasses`, and `affectedSurfacesSeed` from reducer-owned state plus iteration JSONL `findingDetails`; if a field is missing, mark it `UNKNOWN` instead of inferring it from prose\n2069: \n2070:           3. **Active Finding Registry**\n2071:              - Unified registry for active P0/P1/P2 findings\n2072:              - For each: ID, severity, title, dimension, file:line, evidence, impact, fix recommendation, disposition, findingClass, scopeProof, affectedSurfaceHints\n2073: \n2074:           4. **Remediation Workstreams**\n2075:              - Ordered action groups: P0 first, then P1, with P2 advisories separated\n2076: \n2077:           5. **Spec Seed**\n2078:              - Concrete seed bullets for follow-on spec updates\n2079: \n2080:           6. **Plan Seed**\n2081:              - Concrete starter tasks for `/speckit:plan`\n2082: \n2083:            7. **Traceability Status**\n2084:               - Summarize required core protocols first, then applicable overlay protocols\n2085:               - Include status, evidence, and any unresolved drift per protocol\n2086:               - Include `AC_COVERAGE` status for lifecycle-active spec-folder targets: exempt, disabled, pass, or advisory-shortfall, with covered/total and floor when available\n2087: \n2088:           If `resource_map_present` is true, insert **## Resource Map Coverage Gate** after `Traceability Status` with exactly three bullets:\n2089:              - `Entries touched`: count of resource-map paths that appear in applied reports\n2090:              - `Entries not touched`: paths in resource-map not in implementation, labeled `expected-by-scope` or `gap`\n2091:              - `Implementation paths absent from resource-map`: `target_files` in applied reports not on the map\n2092: \n2093:           8. **Deferred Items**\n2094:              - Advisory-only or backlog-worthy follow-ups that do not block the current verdict\n2095: \n2096:           **Dimension Expansion Map**\n2097:              - Insert `## Dimension Expansion Map` after Deferred Items and before Search Ledger.\n2098:              - Render reducer-owned `divergence.saturatedDirections`, completed pivots, failed pivots, audited overrides, Council artifact references, selected review directions, and remaining frontier.\n2099:              - This section records breadth only. It cannot alter the Executive Summary verdict, hasAdvisories, finding registry, or adversarial self-check results.\n2100: \n2101:           9. **Search Ledger**\n2102:              - Always include this section before the appendix.\n2103:              - Render reducer-owned `searchCoverage`, `candidateCoverage`, `searchDebt`, `ruledOutCandidates`, and `cleanSearchProof`.\n2104:              - If all arrays are empty or absent, include: `*No search-depth state captured (legacy v1 record)*`.\n2105:              - When `searchDebt` is non-empty, state hasSearchDebt: true. The verdict already counts it: CONDITIONAL unless an active P0 or a failed gate makes it FAIL. When debt is the only reason for CONDITIONAL, the next step is another /deep:review over the deferred or blocked bug classes, not /speckit:plan.\n2106: \n2107:           10. **Audit Appendix**\n2108:              - Convergence summary, coverage summary, ruled-out claims, sources reviewed\n2109:              - Cross-reference appendix MUST be split into `Core Protocols` and `Overlay Protocols`\n2110: \n2111:           Preserve machine-owned markers so the reducer-owned registry, dashboard, and strategy anchors can be refreshed on re-run without mutating prior synthesis. (Note: `completed-continue` lineage branch is deferred — see `deep-review/references/protocol/loop-protocol.md §Lifecycle Branches`.)\n2112:         output: \"{state_paths.review_output}\"\n2113: \n2114:       step_derive_release_readiness_state:\n2115:         action: \"Bind release-readiness state from final review results\"\n2116:         algorithm: |\n2117:           if active_p0 > 0:\n2118:             release_readiness_state = \"release-blocking\"\n2119:           elif reason == \"converged\" and verdict in [\"PASS\", \"CONDITIONAL\"]:\n2120:             release_readiness_state = \"converged\"\n2121:           else:\n2122:             release_readiness_state = \"in-progress\"\n2123:         outputs:\n2124:           - release_readiness_state: \"in-progress | converged | release-blocking\"\n2125:         note: \"State meanings follow releaseReadinessStates in deep-review/assets/review-mode-contract.yaml.\"\n2126: \n2127:       step_convergence_report:\n2128:         action: \"Append convergence report to JSONL\"\n2129:         dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n2130:         command: |\n2131:           GATEWAY=\".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/append-mode-event.cjs\"\n2132:           [ -f \"$GATEWAY\" ] || GATEWAY=\"scripts/append-mode-event.cjs\"\n2133:           EVENT_DIR=\"$(mktemp -d \"${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/deep-review-synthesis.XXXXXX\")\"\n2134:           CLOSEOUT=\".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/synthesis-closeout.cjs\"\n2135:           [ -f \"$CLOSEOUT\" ] || CLOSEOUT=\"scripts/synthesis-closeout.cjs\"\n2136:           node \"$CLOSEOUT\" --mode review --event-dir \"$EVENT_DIR\" \\\n2137:             --artifact-dir \"{state_paths.packet_dir}\" \\\n2138:             --state-log \"{state_paths.state_log}\" \\\n2139:             --registry \"{state_paths.findings_registry}\" \\\n2140:             --output \"{state_paths.review_output}\" \\\n2141:             --dashboard \"{state_paths.dashboard}\" \\\n2142:             --stop-reason \"{reason}\" \\\n2143:             --active-p0 \"{active_p0}\" --active-p1 \"{active_p1}\" --active-p2 \"{active_p2}\" \\\n2144:             --dimension-coverage \"{dimension_coverage}\" \\\n2145:             --verdict \"{verdict}\" \\\n2146:             --release-readiness-state \"{release_readiness_state}\"\n2147:           NODE_STATUS=$?\n2148:           for eventFile in \"$EVENT_DIR\"/*.json; do\n2149:             [ -e \"$eventFile\" ] || continue\n2150:             node \"$GATEWAY\" --mode review --run-directory \"$(dirname \"{state_paths.state_log}\")\" --event-json \"$eventFile\"\n2151:             GATEWAY_STATUS=$?\n2152:             if [ \"$GATEWAY_STATUS\" -ne 0 ]; then\n2153:               rm -rf \"$EVENT_DIR\"\n2154:               exit \"$GATEWAY_STATUS\"\n2155:             fi\n2156:           done\n2157:           rm -rf \"$EVENT_DIR\"\n2158:           exit \"$NODE_STATUS\"\n2159:         note: \"Emit as numeric ratio (e.g., 0.75), not quoted string. Compute: dimensions_covered / total_dimensions.\"\n2160: \n2161:       step_update_config_status:\n2162:         action: \"Mark config as complete\"\n2163:         dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n2164:         edit: \"{state_paths.config}\"\n2165:         set_field: { status: \"complete\" }\n2166: \n2167:       step_stage_artifact_dir:\n2168:         skip_when: \"config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir is present\"\n2169:         action: \"Stage all skill-owned artifacts under artifact_dir for the operator's next git commit\"\n2170:         dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n2171:         command: \"git add {state_paths.artifact_dir}\"\n2172:         note: \"Staging the whole artifact_dir keeps the iteration trail (iterations/, deltas/, state.jsonl, strategy, findings-registry, and the report) together; the operator keeps commit authority and can `git restore --staged {path}` before committing. Failure is non-fatal -- log warning and continue.\"\n2173:         on_fail: \"Log warning. Do not block synthesis. The artifact_dir may be outside a git repo (e.g., temp test fixture) which is a valid case.\"\n2174: \n2175:       # ─── APPROVAL GATE: Post-Synthesis ───\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 2176]","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":true},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review.yaml, lines 1996-2175\n1996:             active_p0: \"active_p0\"\n1997:             active_p1: \"active_p1\"\n1998:             active_p2: \"active_p2\"\n1999:             search_debt_count: \"search_debt\"\n2000:           on_fail: \"Halt with STATUS=FAIL through step_release_lock. The values the merge bound are the authority on a fan-out root, so an unreadable bound value must stop the run rather than let a verdict be guessed.\"\n2001:         if_absent:\n2002:           command: |\n2003:             node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/review-verdict.cjs \\\n2004:               --registry-path \"{state_paths.findings_registry}\" \\\n2005:               --state-log \"{state_paths.state_log}\"\n2006:           working_directory: \"{repo_root}\"\n2007:           wait_for_completion: true\n2008:           bind_from_output:\n2009:             verdict: \"verdict\"\n2010:             has_advisories: \"has_advisories\"\n2011:             active_p0: \"active_p0\"\n2012:             active_p1: \"active_p1\"\n2013:             active_p2: \"active_p2\"\n2014:             search_debt_count: \"search_debt\"\n2015:           on_fail: \"Halt with STATUS=FAIL through step_release_lock. A non-zero exit means the registry or the state log could not be read, so this stop has no verdict yet and none may be assumed.\"\n2016:         outputs:\n2017:           - verdict: \"PASS | CONDITIONAL | FAIL\"\n2018:           - has_advisories: \"Boolean true when verdict is PASS and any active P2 findings exist\"\n2019:           - active_p0: \"Active P0 count the verdict used\"\n2020:           - active_p1: \"Active P1 count the verdict used\"\n2021:           - active_p2: \"Active P2 count the verdict used\"\n2022:           - ac_coverage_signal: \"exempt | disabled | pass | advisory-shortfall\"\n2023:         contract: |\n2024:           Every iteration-NNN.md must end with exactly: \"Review verdict: PASS\" (or CONDITIONAL or FAIL).\n2025:           Downstream automation parses this final line via exact string match — do not vary the format.\n2026: \n2027:       step_emit_resource_map:\n2028:         skip_when: \"config.fanout is present\"\n2029:         action: \"Emit {state_paths.resource_map_output} from converged review deltas unless config.resource_map.emit is false\"\n2030:         dry_run_boundary: \"reducer-refresh\"\n2031:         command: \"node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/reduce-state.cjs {spec_folder} {reducer_artifact_arg} --create-missing-anchors --emit-resource-map\"\n2032:         read:\n2033:           - \"{state_paths.config}\"\n2034:           - \"{state_paths.delta_dir}/iter-*.jsonl\"\n2035:         write:\n2036:           - \"{state_paths.resource_map_output}\"\n2037:         guarantee: \"Reducer skips cleanly when config.resource_map.emit == false and writes a deterministic resource-map when enabled.\"\n2038:         note: \"A fan-out root has no root state log before closeout, so the root reducer would fail on the missing file. Each lineage emits its own map, so the report names the ones that exist at {artifact_dir}/lineages/*/resource-map.md.\"\n2039: \n2040:       step_resource_map_coverage_gate:\n2041:         action: \"If resource_map_present, compute the Resource Map Coverage Gate synthesis inputs; otherwise preserve the skip note\"\n2042:         note: \"Cross-check target_files from {spec_folder}/applied/T-*.md against {spec_folder}/resource-map.md. Report touched entries, untouched entries split into expected-by-scope vs gap, and implementation paths absent from the map. Findings raised here use category resource-map-coverage with severity calibrated to the gate outcome.\"\n2043: \n2044:       step_compile_review_report:\n2045:         action: \"Compile review/review-report.md with 9 core sections, a conditional Resource Map Coverage Gate section, and an embedded Planning Packet\"\n2046:         dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n2047:         instructions: |\n2048:           **Zero-iteration stop:** When {state_paths.state_log} holds no line with type \"iteration\" (on a fan-out root, when none of the lineage state logs under {state_paths.packet_dir}/lineages/ holds one), the review did not run, and the report says so instead of reporting on work that never happened:\n2049:              - Executive Summary: open with `Review did not run`, state the stop reason and `0 iterations dispatched`, keep the verdict and hasAdvisories bound by step_derive_verdict unchanged, and state that the P0/P1/P2 counts mean not examined rather than clean.\n2050:              - Planning Trigger: state that `/speckit:plan` is not required, and set the Planning Packet to `triggered: false` and `reviewDidNotRun: true` with `remediationWorkstreams: []`, keeping every other required key from section 2 at an empty value.\n2051:              - Next step: name `/deep:review` again with a duration budget or iteration cap that allows at least one pass.\n2052:              - Sections 3 to 8: give each a single line saying the review did not run.\n2053: \n2054:           Create review/review-report.md with the following sections:\n2055: \n2056:           1. **Executive Summary**\n2057:              - Overall verdict: PASS | CONDITIONAL | FAIL\n2058:              - hasAdvisories: true when PASS carries active P2 items\n2059:              - P0/P1/P2 counts: {active_p0}, {active_p1}, {active_p2}, the counts the verdict used, stated as such\n2060:              - Self-check outcomes: each finding the adversarial self-check confirmed, downgraded or called a false positive. On a single-executor run the counts above already reflect them, so list them for reference\n2061:              - Review scope summary\n2062:              - Operator review focus: config.reviewFocus verbatim, or omit this line when it is null\n2063: \n2064:           2. **Planning Trigger**\n2065:              - State whether `/speckit:plan` is required\n2066:              - Include a fenced `json` block labeled `Planning Packet`\n2067:              - The packet MUST include: `triggered`, `verdict`, `hasAdvisories`, `activeFindings`, `remediationWorkstreams`, `specSeed`, `planSeed`, `findingClasses`, `affectedSurfacesSeed`, `fixCompletenessRequired`\n2068:              - Build `activeFindings`, `findingClasses`, and `affectedSurfacesSeed` from reducer-owned state plus iteration JSONL `findingDetails`; if a field is missing, mark it `UNKNOWN` instead of inferring it from prose\n2069: \n2070:           3. **Active Finding Registry**\n2071:              - Unified registry for active P0/P1/P2 findings\n2072:              - For each: ID, severity, title, dimension, file:line, evidence, impact, fix recommendation, disposition, findingClass, scopeProof, affectedSurfaceHints\n2073: \n2074:           4. **Remediation Workstreams**\n2075:              - Ordered action groups: P0 first, then P1, with P2 advisories separated\n2076: \n2077:           5. **Spec Seed**\n2078:              - Concrete seed bullets for follow-on spec updates\n2079: \n2080:           6. **Plan Seed**\n2081:              - Concrete starter tasks for `/speckit:plan`\n2082: \n2083:            7. **Traceability Status**\n2084:               - Summarize required core protocols first, then applicable overlay protocols\n2085:               - Include status, evidence, and any unresolved drift per protocol\n2086:               - Include `AC_COVERAGE` status for lifecycle-active spec-folder targets: exempt, disabled, pass, or advisory-shortfall, with covered/total and floor when available\n2087: \n2088:           If `resource_map_present` is true, insert **## Resource Map Coverage Gate** after `Traceability Status` with exactly three bullets:\n2089:              - `Entries touched`: count of resource-map paths that appear in applied reports\n2090:              - `Entries not touched`: paths in resource-map not in implementation, labeled `expected-by-scope` or `gap`\n2091:              - `Implementation paths absent from resource-map`: `target_files` in applied reports not on the map\n2092: \n2093:           8. **Deferred Items**\n2094:              - Advisory-only or backlog-worthy follow-ups that do not block the current verdict\n2095: \n2096:           **Dimension Expansion Map**\n2097:              - Insert `## Dimension Expansion Map` after Deferred Items and before Search Ledger.\n2098:              - Render reducer-owned `divergence.saturatedDirections`, completed pivots, failed pivots, audited overrides, Council artifact references, selected review directions, and remaining frontier.\n2099:              - This section records breadth only. It cannot alter the Executive Summary verdict, hasAdvisories, finding registry, or adversarial self-check results.\n2100: \n2101:           9. **Search Ledger**\n2102:              - Always include this section before the appendix.\n2103:              - Render reducer-owned `searchCoverage`, `candidateCoverage`, `searchDebt`, `ruledOutCandidates`, and `cleanSearchProof`.\n2104:              - If all arrays are empty or absent, include: `*No search-depth state captured (legacy v1 record)*`.\n2105:              - When `searchDebt` is non-empty, state hasSearchDebt: true. The verdict already counts it: CONDITIONAL unless an active P0 or a failed gate makes it FAIL. When debt is the only reason for CONDITIONAL, the next step is another /deep:review over the deferred or blocked bug classes, not /speckit:plan.\n2106: \n2107:           10. **Audit Appendix**\n2108:              - Convergence summary, coverage summary, ruled-out claims, sources reviewed\n2109:              - Cross-reference appendix MUST be split into `Core Protocols` and `Overlay Protocols`\n2110: \n2111:           Preserve machine-owned markers so the reducer-owned registry, dashboard, and strategy anchors can be refreshed on re-run without mutating prior synthesis. (Note: `completed-continue` lineage branch is deferred — see `deep-review/references/protocol/loop-protocol.md §Lifecycle Branches`.)\n2112:         output: \"{state_paths.review_output}\"\n2113: \n2114:       step_derive_release_readiness_state:\n2115:         action: \"Bind release-readiness state from final review results\"\n2116:         algorithm: |\n2117:           if active_p0 > 0:\n2118:             release_readiness_state = \"release-blocking\"\n2119:           elif reason == \"converged\" and verdict in [\"PASS\", \"CONDITIONAL\"]:\n2120:             release_readiness_state = \"converged\"\n2121:           else:\n2122:             release_readiness_state = \"in-progress\"\n2123:         outputs:\n2124:           - release_readiness_state: \"in-progress | converged | release-blocking\"\n2125:         note: \"State meanings follow releaseReadinessStates in deep-review/assets/review-mode-contract.yaml.\"\n2126: \n2127:       step_convergence_report:\n2128:         action: \"Append convergence report to JSONL\"\n2129:         dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n2130:         command: |\n2131:           GATEWAY=\".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/append-mode-event.cjs\"\n2132:           [ -f \"$GATEWAY\" ] || GATEWAY=\"scripts/append-mode-event.cjs\"\n2133:           EVENT_DIR=\"$(mktemp -d \"${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/deep-review-synthesis.XXXXXX\")\"\n2134:           CLOSEOUT=\".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/synthesis-closeout.cjs\"\n2135:           [ -f \"$CLOSEOUT\" ] || CLOSEOUT=\"scripts/synthesis-closeout.cjs\"\n2136:           node \"$CLOSEOUT\" --mode review --event-dir \"$EVENT_DIR\" \\\n2137:             --artifact-dir \"{state_paths.packet_dir}\" \\\n2138:             --state-log \"{state_paths.state_log}\" \\\n2139:             --registry \"{state_paths.findings_registry}\" \\\n2140:             --output \"{state_paths.review_output}\" \\\n2141:             --dashboard \"{state_paths.dashboard}\" \\\n2142:             --stop-reason \"{reason}\" \\\n2143:             --active-p0 \"{active_p0}\" --active-p1 \"{active_p1}\" --active-p2 \"{active_p2}\" \\\n2144:             --dimension-coverage \"{dimension_coverage}\" \\\n2145:             --verdict \"{verdict}\" \\\n2146:             --release-readiness-state \"{release_readiness_state}\"\n2147:           NODE_STATUS=$?\n2148:           for eventFile in \"$EVENT_DIR\"/*.json; do\n2149:             [ -e \"$eventFile\" ] || continue\n2150:             node \"$GATEWAY\" --mode review --run-directory \"$(dirname \"{state_paths.state_log}\")\" --event-json \"$eventFile\"\n2151:             GATEWAY_STATUS=$?\n2152:             if [ \"$GATEWAY_STATUS\" -ne 0 ]; then\n2153:               rm -rf \"$EVENT_DIR\"\n2154:               exit \"$GATEWAY_STATUS\"\n2155:             fi\n2156:           done\n2157:           rm -rf \"$EVENT_DIR\"\n2158:           exit \"$NODE_STATUS\"\n2159:         note: \"Emit as numeric ratio (e.g., 0.75), not quoted string. Compute: dimensions_covered / total_dimensions.\"\n2160: \n2161:       step_update_config_status:\n2162:         action: \"Mark config as complete\"\n2163:         dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n2164:         edit: \"{state_paths.config}\"\n2165:         set_field: { status: \"complete\" }\n2166: \n2167:       step_stage_artifact_dir:\n2168:         skip_when: \"config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir is present\"\n2169:         action: \"Stage all skill-owned artifacts under artifact_dir for the operator's next git commit\"\n2170:         dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n2171:         command: \"git add {state_paths.artifact_dir}\"\n2172:         note: \"Staging the whole artifact_dir keeps the iteration trail (iterations/, deltas/, state.jsonl, strategy, findings-registry, and the report) together; the operator keeps commit authority and can `git restore --staged {path}` before committing. Failure is non-fatal -- log warning and continue.\"\n2173:         on_fail: \"Log warning. Do not block synthesis. The artifact_dir may be outside a git repo (e.g., temp test fixture) which is a valid case.\"\n2174: \n2175:       # ─── APPROVAL GATE: Post-Synthesis ───\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 2176]"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"limit\":180,\"offset\":1996,\"path\":\".skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review.yaml\"}"},"time":{"start":1794853182087,"end":1794853182556}}}}
