{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794853287479,"sessionID":"ses_e1a82d918ffeSg4o2dc6d2Zt3H","part":{"partID":"prt_1e597b488001CvmAgmovSzjWdo","sessionID":"ses_e1a82d918ffeSg4o2dc6d2Zt3H","messageID":"msg_1e5978e79001dmB52f5nvnjEBQ","type":"tool","id":"call_f0f72d1d90aa426e873b664d","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"limit":120,"offset":2176,"path":".skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review.yaml"},"output":"Read file .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review.yaml, lines 2176-2295\n2176:       gate_post_synthesis:\n2177:         applies_to: confirm\n2178:         type: approval_gate\n2179:         purpose: \"Show review/review-report.md summary and get approval\"\n2180:         present: |\n2181:           ## Review Synthesis Complete\n2182: \n2183:           **review/review-report.md** has been compiled with findings from {iteration_count} iterations.\n2184:           **Verdict**: {verdict} | **hasAdvisories**: {has_advisories}\n2185:           **Active Findings**: P0={active_p0} P1={active_p1} P2={active_p2}\n2186:           **Dimension Coverage**: {dimension_coverage}\n2187: \n2188:           Review `{state_paths.review_output}` before deciding next steps.\n2189: \n2190:           Options:\n2191:           A) Approve and save to memory\n2192:           B) Generate remediation plan (creates action items for /speckit:plan)\n2193:           C) Request revisions to review/review-report.md\n2194:           D) Skip memory save\n2195:         wait_for: \"User response\"\n2196:         after_gate_refresh_lock: gate_defaults.after_gate_refresh_lock\n2197:         on_A: { proceed_to: phase_save }\n2198:         on_B: { action: \"Generate remediation plan section, then save to memory\", proceed_to: phase_save }\n2199:         on_C: { action: \"Apply user revisions\", return_to: gate_post_synthesis }\n2200:         on_D: { proceed_to: completion }\n2201: \n2202:   # ════════\n2203:   # PHASE 4: SAVE\n2204:   # ════════\n2205:   phase_save:\n2206:     purpose: Preserve review context in packet continuity\n2207:     steps:\n2208: \n2209:       step_compose_save_payload:\n2210:         action: \"Compose the structured JSON payload consumed by generate-context.js\"\n2211:         dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n2212:         output: \"/tmp/save-context-data-<session-id>.json\"\n2213:         requirements:\n2214:           - \"Write this file before invoking generate-context.js; the loader fails closed if the explicit JSON file is absent.\"\n2215:           - \"Include `specFolder`, a concise `sessionSummary`, curated `observations`, `recent_context`, `toolCalls`, and `exchanges` from the completed review loop. Without `--full-auto` the writer only plans, and a full-auto save writes continuity only from `recent_action`, `next_safe_action`, `blockers` and `key_files`, so the payload carries all four.\"\n2216:           - \"Use a session-scoped temp filename; do not use the retired shared `/tmp/save-context-data.json` path.\"\n2217:         example_payload: |\n2218:           {\n2219:             \"specFolder\": \"{spec_folder}\",\n2220:             \"sessionSummary\": \"Deep review completed; see review/review-report.md for verdict, findings, and workstreams.\",\n2221:             \"observations\": [\"Summarize the active findings, verdict, and remediation guidance.\"],\n2222:             \"recent_context\": [\"Point to the generated review artifacts and next action.\"],\n2223:             \"exchanges\": [],\n2224:             \"toolCalls\": [],\n2225:             \"recent_action\": \"Deep review finished with verdict {verdict} after {iteration_count} iterations\",\n2226:             \"next_safe_action\": \"Act on the verdict in review/review-report.md\",\n2227:             \"blockers\": [],\n2228:             \"key_files\": [\"review/review-report.md\"]\n2229:           }\n2230: \n2231:       step_generate_context:\n2232:         action: \"Route continuity content into the correct canonical spec document via generate-context.js\"\n2233:         dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n2234:         command: \"node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/dist/continuity/generate-context.js /tmp/save-context-data-<session-id>.json {spec_folder} --full-auto\"\n2235:         critical_rule: \"NEVER manually author files under retired memory/ paths (the runtime rejects them); use generate-context.js so the save routes into decision-record.md, implementation-summary.md, or handover.md\"\n2236: \n2237:       step_verify_save:\n2238:         action: \"Verify canonical save routed content into the correct spec document\"\n2239:         check: \"Does {spec_folder}/implementation-summary.md, {spec_folder}/decision-record.md, or {spec_folder}/handover.md carry the new continuity update?\"\n2240:         on_fail: \"Log warning but do not block completion\"\n2241: \n2242:       step_release_lock:\n2243:         action: \"Release the single-writer lock after save, skip-save, or cancellation cleanup has resolved\"\n2244:         dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n2245:         command: \"node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/loop-lock.cjs release --lock-path {state_paths.lock_file} --owner-pid {captured_owner_pid} --nonce {captured_acquire_nonce}\"\n2246:         bookkeeping_log: '{\"type\":\"event\",\"event\":\"lock_released\",\"path\":\"{state_paths.lock_file}\",\"releasePhase\":\"save\",\"timestamp\":\"{ISO_8601_NOW}\"}'\n2247: \n2248:   # ════════\n2249:   # COMPLETION\n2250:   # ════════\n2251:   completion:\n2252:     message: |\n2253:       Deep review complete.\n2254:       Iterations: {iteration_count} | Stop reason: {reason}\n2255:       Findings: P0={active_p0} P1={active_p1} P2={active_p2}\n2256:       Verdict: {verdict} | hasAdvisories={has_advisories}\n2257: \n2258:       Artifacts:\n2259:         - review/review-report.md (compiled from {iteration_count} iterations)\n2260:         - {iteration_count} iteration files in review/iterations/\n2261:         - State files in review/: deep-review-config.json, deep-review-state.jsonl, deep-review-findings-registry.json, deep-review-strategy.md, deep-review-dashboard.md\n2262:         - Memory context saved\n2263: \n2264:       STATUS=OK PATH={spec_folder}\n2265:     next_steps:\n2266:       - \"/speckit:plan [remediation] (if FAIL or CONDITIONAL verdict)\"\n2267:       - \"/create:changelog (if PASS, including PASS with hasAdvisories=true)\"\n2268:       - \"/deep:review [target] (for another review)\"\n2269:       - \"/speckit:save {spec_folder} (refresh canonical continuity before the next session)\"\n2270: \n2271: # ────────\n2272: # ERROR RECOVERY\n2273: # ────────\n2274: error_recovery:\n2275:   agent_dispatch_timeout: \"Retry once with reduced scope (fewer files per iteration). If second timeout, mark as 'timeout' and continue.\"\n2276:   state_file_missing: \"If JSONL missing during loop, reconstruct from iteration files. If strategy missing, create minimal version.\"\n2277:   consecutive_failures: \"See step_check_convergence rule 1a. The script counts trailing failed iterations from the state log and returns stop reason error.\"\n2278:   continuity_save_failure: \"Preserve the review packet in review/ as backup. Log warning.\"\n2279: \n2280: # ────────\n2281: # RULES\n2282: # ────────\n2283: rules:\n2284:   DRY_RUN_OVERRIDES:\n2285:     - \"When dry_run is true, dry_run_control overrides default dispatch, write, reducer, continuity-save, and child-spawn requirements.\"\n2286:     - \"Dry-run preview events are emitted to terminal output only and are not persisted.\"\n2287:   ALWAYS:\n2288:     - follow_workflow_phases_in_order\n2289:     - dispatch_deep_review_agent_per_iteration\n2290:     - check_convergence_before_each_iteration\n2291:     - write_all_state_to_files\n2292:     - write_continuity_after_synthesis\n2293:     - respect_max_iterations_cap\n2294:     - treat_review_target_as_read_only\n2295:     - deduplicate_findings_before_synthesis\n[Output truncated. Conti