{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794853403010,"sessionID":"ses_e1a82d918ffeSg4o2dc6d2Zt3H","part":{"partID":"prt_1e5997142001IzcC5Lx9RUEtUS","sessionID":"ses_e1a82d918ffeSg4o2dc6d2Zt3H","messageID":"msg_1e5995658001IAHXxb86t8CkN0","type":"tool","id":"call_25462214be6f46aba0c6da9f","tool":"edit","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"newString":"`review-verdict.cjs` returns FAIL with `failed_required_gate_ids: [\"coverage\"]`: 0 P0 and 2 P1 are active, and the coverage gate is failing because both core protocols are `partial`. The finding counts alone would map to CONDITIONAL, so every iteration's final line says CONDITIONAL; the synthesis verdict is recomputed with the terminal gates and is the release-facing one. WS-1 and WS-3 are the work that clears the finding side; a protocol pass is the work that clears the gate.","oldString":"`review-verdict.cjs` returned CONDITIONAL from the registry (0 P0, 2 P1, 5 P2). The terminal stop also recorded `dimensionCoverageGate` as a blocker and both core protocols are `partial`, so the release decision should treat the traceability evidence as unresolved until WS-1 and WS-3 land.","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/fixes-11/review-report.md"},"output":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/fixes-11/review-report.md (1 replacement)","title":"edit","metadata":{"metadata":{"files":[{"file":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/fixes-11/review-report.md","patch":"Index: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/fixes-11/review-report.md\n===================================================================\n--- specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/fixes-11/review-report.md\n+++ specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/fixes-11/review-report.md\n@@ -224,9 +224,9 @@\n All four overlay protocols are `notApplicable` for this scope, with the reasons in section 7.\n \n ### Caveat for the release decision\n \n-`review-verdict.cjs` returned CONDITIONAL from the registry (0 P0, 2 P1, 5 P2). The terminal stop also recorded `dimensionCoverageGate` as a blocker and both core protocols are `partial`, so the release decision should treat the traceability evidence as unresolved until WS-1 and WS-3 land.\n+`review-verdict.cjs` returns FAIL with `failed_required_gate_ids: [\"coverage\"]`: 0 P0 and 2 P1 are active, and the coverage gate is failing because both core protocols are `partial`. The finding counts alone would map to CONDITIONAL, so every iteration's final line says CONDITIONAL; the synthesis verdict is recomputed with the terminal gates and is the release-facing one. WS-1 and WS-3 are the work that clears the finding side; a protocol pass is the work that clears the gate.\n \n ### Holdout hygiene\n \n No holdout prompt text was read or printed at any point; no command-prompt corpus was opened, and the holdout gate was read by count only.\n","status":"modified","additions":1,"deletions":1}],"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/fixes-11/review-report.md (1 replacement)"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"newString\":\"`review-verdict.cjs` returns FAIL with `failed_required_gate_ids: [\\\"coverage\\\"]`: 0 P0 and 2 P1 are active, and the coverage gate is failing because both core protocols are `partial`. The finding counts alone would map to CONDITIONAL, so every iteration's final line says CONDITIONAL; the synthesis verdict is recomputed with the terminal gates and is the release-facing one. WS-1 and WS-3 are the work that clears the finding side; a protocol pass is the work that clears the gate.\",\"oldString\":\"`review-verdict.cjs` returned CONDITIONAL from the registry (0 P0, 2 P1, 5 P2). The terminal stop also recorded `dimensionCoverageGate` as a blocker and both core protocols are `partial`, so the release decision should treat the traceability evidence as unresolved until WS-1 and WS-3 land.\",\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/fixes-11/review-report.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794853400898,"end":1794853403010}}}}
